    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/assistant-director-athletic-marketing-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing 497734 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Division: 6R1000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G20 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dusty Ridner Job Summary/Basic Functions The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's Degree. Experience: One year of work related experience in intercollegiate athletics. Job Duties: 40% - Implement and Execute Marketing Plans. Follow and hit deadlines within current marketing plan to allow Athletics the best opportunity to succeed and increase attendance numbers significantly. - (Essential) 25% - Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. - (Essential) 20% - Community Relationships and Group Sales. Responsible for creating and maintaining relationships within the community and turning that into revenue generation through group sales, group experiences, or season tickets. - (Essential) 10% - Game Day Operations Support. Support marketing efforts during the game day experience for all home sports. - (Essential) 5% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 58ed13fb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics 90R000 - Intercol