    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/executive-director-marketing-strategy-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Marketing Strategy",
      "description": "Executive Director, Marketing Strategy - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Executive Director, Marketing Strategy - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Executive Director, Marketing Strategy 497782 Richmond Campus Management Positions Marketing Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Some evenings and weekends required. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G28 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dan Hendrickson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master’s degree in Digital Marketing, Web Development, Communications, Higher Education Administration, or a related field is required. Experience: Three years of experience is required. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 45% - Collaborate with the VP to shape and execute EKU’s multi-year marketing and digital strategy in alignment with brand strategy as set by Communications and Brand Management. Serve as Deputy Chief Marketing Officer, acting as the primary delegate in the VP’s absence. Translate institutional priorities into marketing campaigns that advance enrollment, retention, fundraising, alumni engagement, and community impact. Lead cross-channel strategies (digital, print, media, social, video, web) that elevate EKU’s visibility and reputation regionally and nationally. Ensure tone, and visual standards are upheld across all units of the University. - (Essential) 30% - Direct planning, development, and execution of integrated campaigns that support enrollment goals, student success, and institutional reputation. Partner with Enrollment Management to create campaigns that drive awareness, applications, and yield across diverse student populations (undergraduate, graduate, online, transfer, adult learners). Collaborate with Advancement and Alumni Relations to design campaigns that strengthen donor and alumni engagement. Use research and analytics to identify target audiences, track performance, and optimize strategies. - (Essential) 25% - Oversee market research, competitor analysis, and enrollment perception studies to guide strategy. Ensure the use of analytics and KPIs to measure campaign ROI and effectiveness. Provide reports and insights to senior leadership on marketing performance and impact. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective a