    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-faculty-paralegal-program-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Paralegal Program",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, Paralegal Program - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-time Faculty, Paralegal Program - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-time Faculty, Paralegal Program 497787 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Apr 6 2027 - 23:55 EDT Title: Part-time Faculty/Online Facilitator, Paralegal Program Position Type: Part-time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part-Time Retirement: None Contact Person: Lynnette Noblitt Job Summary/Basic Functions The Eastern Kentucky University Department of Government is accepting applications for adjunct faculty positions/online course facilitator in Paralegal Science. Successful candidates will teach/facilitate courses in Legal Research & Writing and Litigation Skills. Candidates should describe legal expertise in these areas and experience working with paralegals in their cover letter and/or CV. These courses will be taught online using the Canvas learning management system and synchronous Zoom every-other Thursday evening, 5-10pm (Eastern Time Zone). A juris doctorate (JD) is required for this position. Previous undergraduate teaching experience, especially in online learning settings, is preferred. Application review will begin October 20, 2026 until position is filled. Minimum Qualifications Education: Candidates must hold a J.D. degree, be licensed to practice law, be eligible for admission to the Kentucky Bar Association, have previous experience supervising paralegals, and able to teach law specific to Kentucky. The candidate's undergraduate degree must be from a regionally accredited institution and the J.D. degree from an ABA accredited law school. Experience: Previous teaching experience at the post-secondary level is preferred. Candidates must hold a J.D. degree, be licensed to practice law, be eligible for admission to the Kentucky Bar Association, have previous experience supervising paralegals, and able to teach law specific to Kentucky. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 64248e62 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) ba99f2a9 Last Name (required) 2b751440 Email (required) b3cfb14d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that