    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/senior-counselor-college-enrollment-and-career-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Counselor, College Enrollment and Career",
      "description": "Senior Counselor, College Enrollment and Career - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Senior Counselor, College Enrollment and Career - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Senior Counselor, College Enrollment and Career 497765 Richmond Campus Academic Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Senior Counselor, College Enrollment and Career Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Some evenings and weekends required. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G20 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Jessica Bailey Job Summary/Basic Functions Senior Counselor for College Enrollment & Career Readiness for the College of Education and Applied Human Sciences provides integrated enrollment support and career readiness coaching for students within assigned academic colleges. This role supports prospective, admitted, and enrolled students by connecting academic programs to career pathways, assisting with enrollment engagement, and delivering career preparation services. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Counseling, Psychology, Social Work, Higher Education, or a related field is required. Master’s degree preferred in Counseling, Higher Education Administration, Social Work, or Student Affairs. Experience can be substituted for specific degree requirements but not educational level. Occasional travel and evening/weekend work may be required for enrollment and engagement events. Experience: Minimum two years of experience in recruitment, student success, career coaching, counseling, crisis intervention, or academic support services is required. Experience working with at-risk student populations, retention initiatives, or case management is referred. Strong understanding of data-informed recruitment, student development, academic advising, and persistence strategies. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 25% - Enrollment & Yield Support. Utilize Slate CRM to manage and track the recruitment process efficiently, ensuring accurate and up-to-date documentation of all interactions. Analyze data and metrics to identify trends, challenges, and opportunities to enhance recruitment strategies. Establish and maintain strong relationships with prospective students, families, and high schools, emphasizing the unique value of the college you represent and providing guidance and support through the Admissions process as their main point of contact.-Assist the Dual Credit team in creating classroom presentations with interactive activities that highlight the College, as well as inviting Faculty to participate in presentations to create buy-in with students. Works with first-year, transfer, and returning students to ensure a smooth transition to EKU, identifying and addressing adjustment challenges. Assists students with navigating university policies, academic resources, and financial aid options prior to move-in and/or the start of classes. - (Essential) 25% - Career Coaching & Career Services. Tailor one-on-one counseling sessions to address individual academic and career aspirations, ensuring a solid fit between the student and the college. Provides structured coaching sessions, workshops, and engagement programming focused on goal setting, career development, and career readiness. Schedule and conduct resume critiques, mock interviewing, and other in-class and out-of-class career readiness services and profile building activities, networking events, and career exploration opportunities. Provide job search tools and strategies. - (Essential) 15% - Experiential Learning Promotion. Promotes internships, co-ops, and experiential learning opportunities Ensure educational success of students in co-op and internships by meeting with students to research and apply for co-ops/internships, serving as a resource for students to solve problems, advising students on requirements of co-ops and internships, and consulting with departments to ensure completion. Manage the co-op and internship process to ensure students, faculty and employers are educated about co-ops and internship process, opportunities and assignments. - (Essential) 15% - Employer & Career Platform Engagement. Establish and cultivate relationships with target employers and organizations to enhance student/alumni employment opportunities. Assists with coordinating job fairs and other employer related events and outreach initiatives by developing college specific marketing strategies and materials. - (Essential) 10% - College Liaison Role. Develop and maintain strong relationships with college deans, departments and faculty to foster a deep knowledge of the academic college and its programs, the related-industry and career outcomes, and support services within the college. Assist with the development of college specific orientation programming. Collaborates with faculty and college leadership on student success initiatives. - (Essential) 10% - Outreach & Events. Host engaging virtual and in-person events, including college-specific information sessions and workshops, to showcase academic programs and foster excitement among prospective students. Utilize various digital platforms to connect with prospective students, showcase the college's academic programs, and facilitate seamless communication throughout the admissions journey. Travel to college fairs, recruitment events, high schools, etc. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 21a06a83 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 6c12b8ff Last Name (required) ab9e9e34 Email (required) fbbd59b2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan ex