      "description": "Coordinator, Administrative - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Coordinator, Administrative - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Coordinator, Administrative 497736 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Fulltime Staff Title: Coordinator, Administrative Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Non-Exempt - G17 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Brooke Bentley Job Summary/Basic Functions Provide high level administration and professional support services for all activities of the program, direct executive assistance to program leaders, and oversee program needs. Services provided include written communications, meeting and resource management, data management and analysis, scheduling, organization, and coordination of activities across departments within EKU to ensure a positive employee experience and seamless service. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree is required Experience: One year of responsible clerical, customer services, and secretarial and/or administrative support is required. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 30% - Communicate with internal and external customers and management to exchange information, resolve issues or concerns, and coordinate activities. - () 5% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned - () 5% - Event planning - (Essential) 10% - Administrative support with student admissions and readmissions - (Essential) 15% - Administrative support utilizing programs such as Word, Excel, Qualtrics, Slate - (Essential) 15% - Administrative support with monitoring of student information and program requirements - (Essential) 15% - Administrative support with examination platforms utilized by the department - (Essential) 5% - Administrative support with administration of departmental course evaluations - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 8584e1bf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 24R000 - College of Health Sciences 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) ca3921e8 Last Name (required) bf0ba8ed Email (required) 2b9e9415 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The 