    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-faculty-aslie-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty, ASLIE",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty, ASLIE - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-Time Faculty, ASLIE - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-Time Faculty, ASLIE 497789 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Dec 4 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Part-Time Faculty, ASLIE Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Contact Person: Carissa Brown Job Summary/Basic Functions The ASL & Interpreter programs within the Department of Language, Cultural Studies, Anthropology & Sociology at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach ASL or Interpreter courses. The courses may include, but are not limited to: ASL 390 Contrastive Analysis: ASL and English. (3 Credits) in a 100% online, synchronous format. To be considered to teach undergraduate level courses, applicants should hold an earned Master's degree in Linguistics, ASL Teaching, or Interpretation from a regionally accredited or internationally recognized institution is required for consideration. Preference for experience teaching post-secondary linguistics using ASL as the language of instruction, particularly the linguistics of signed languages. Part-time faculty may teach up to nine credit hours, depending on departmental needs. Applicants will be screened and contacted as departmental needs for part-time faculty arise. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master's degree in Linguistics, ASL Teaching, or Interpretation from a regionally accredited or internationally recognized institution is required for consideration. Preference for experience teaching post-secondary linguistics using ASL as the language of instruction, particularly the linguistics of signed languages. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Applicant documents include: Identify potential application documents. (May include the following, as appropriate.) • Cover Letter • Vitae • Copies of unofficial transcripts • Contact Information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c980e6ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) e5a0634c Last Name (required) b040acd9 Email (required) 13d89f69 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, 