    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/analyst-marketing-engagement-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-6ae12c58-7afe-48ec-98f2-b9759e4221cf": {
      "title": "Analyst, Marketing & Engagement",
      "description": "Analyst, Marketing & Engagement - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Analyst, Marketing & Engagement - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Analyst, Marketing & Engagement 497781 Richmond Campus Marketing Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Analyst, Marketing & Engagement Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 37.5 Additional Schedule Details: Some evenings and weekends required. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G23 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dan Hendrickson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Marketing & Engagement Analyst is responsible for analyzing, measuring, and optimizing EKU’s student recruitment and engagement efforts. This role plays a key part in data-driven decision-making, ensuring marketing campaigns, digital engagement strategies, and student outreach efforts are highly effective, targeted, and continuously refined. Working closely with the Marketing Strategy, Digital Experience & Creative, and Communications & Content teams, the Marketing & Engagement Analyst uses data to evaluate campaign performance, audience behavior, and conversion trends, providing insights that enhance EKU’s enrollment, retention, and student success initiatives. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Data Analytics, Marketing, Business, Communications, or a related field. Master’s degree preferred. Experience: Experience can be substituted for specific degree requirements but not educational level. Minimum two years of experience in marketing analytics, digital engagement analysis, CRM data reporting, or market research. Experience with Technolutions Slate or similar CRM platforms preferred. Strong background in data visualization, performance tracking, and predictive analytics. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 40% - Monitors and analyzes marketing and student engagement metrics across digital platforms, CRM campaigns, email marketing, social media, and paid advertising. Develops dashboards and reports using Technolutions Slate, Google Analytics, CRM data, and other analytics tools to track campaign effectiveness, audience engagement, and conversion rates. Provides actionable insights to optimize marketing and recruitment strategies, ensuring continuous improvement. - (Essential) 30% - Conducts research on prospective student behaviors, trends in higher education marketing, and competitive positioning to inform marketing strategy. Uses data-driven methodologies to develop audience segmentation models, personas, and engagement strategies for targeted marketing. Analyzes retention and persistence data to identify key touchpoints for engagement and communication. - (Essential) 20% - Works with the Marketing Strategy team to implement A/B testing, automation workflows, and behavioral triggers to improve engagement and conversion rates. Assesses email, web, and digital ad performance, recommending refinements based on data insights. Monitors engagement trends and adjusts marketing strategies based on real-time analytics. - (Essential) 10% - Partners with Admissions, Enrollment Management, Student Success, and Institutional Research to ensure data alignment and strategic decision-making. Supports the Associate Director in marketing performance reviews and strategic planning efforts. Recommends process improvements to enhance data collection, reporting, and analytics integration within marketing workflows. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7d529f83 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 7a3965db Last Name (required) 1395d0e2 Email (required) fde46a81 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall