    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-secondary-instructor-dept-chemistry-and-forensic-science-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part-Time Secondary Instructor, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science",
      "description": "Part-Time Secondary Instructor, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-Time Secondary Instructor, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-Time Secondary Instructor, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science 497784 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Part-Time Secondary Instructor, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Additional Schedule Details: Appointments will begin this Fall 2026 semester, with options to renew on a semester-to-semester basis. Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: Rachel Velez Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science at EKU is seeking a Part-Time Secondary Instructor to work with program faculty, assisting in teaching undergraduate lectures and laboratories. Appointment will begin this Fall 2026 semester, with options to renew on a semester-to-semester basis, as available. Course load may be up to 9 credit hours per semester, depending on need. Courses may include, but are not limited to: Introductory Chemistry, General Chemistry, Organic Chemistry, Analytic Chemistry, associated labs, and any other chemistry and/or forensic science course offered by the department. Candidates must have a minimum of a bachelor's degree in Chemistry or a related discipline, or hold a bachelor's degree and at least 18 graduate credit hours in Chemistry or a related discipline. Degree(s) must be from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution. Candidates will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate programs, and contact information for at least 3 professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Applicants will be screened and contacted as departmental needs for part-time faculty arise. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis. Minimum Qualifications Education: Candidates must have a minimum of a bachelor's degree in Chemistry or a related discipline, or hold a bachelor's degree and at least 18 graduate credit hours in Chemistry or a related discipline. Degree(s) must be from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution. Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 100%% - Teach courses as assigned at the times and in the locations necessary to meet the needs of EKU students - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: Applicant documents include: • Cover Letter • Vitae • Copies of unofficial transcripts • Contact Information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e7ed9be3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 5c520079 Last Name (required) 1681a41b Email (required) 072ea1fa Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organiza