    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-enrollment-management-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management 497715 Richmond Campus Management Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Some evenings and weekends required. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G29 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dan Hendrickson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management is EKU's senior operating officer for new student enrollment across every population the institution serves. The AVP EM is accountable for delivering new student headcount, net tuition revenue, and class profile targets, and for the operational systems that convert interest into enrolled students. The portfolio pairs recruitment across all populations with financial aid strategy and administration. That pairing is deliberate. At a regional comprehensive serving high concentrations of first-generation, rural, transfer, and adult students, award timing and affordability clarity are yield levers, not back-office functions. Separating them from recruitment produces exactly the handoff friction that loses students between admit and enroll. This is an outcomes role. The successful candidate is an enrollment operations executive who can hold a funnel target and run a Title IV compliance shop with equal seriousness. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Counseling, Public Administration, or a related field Experience: Five years of progressive leadership experience in enrollment management, admissions, or financial aid, including at least three years supervising professional staff at the director level or above. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 25% - Own annual and multi-year new student targets across first-time full-time, transfer, adult, online, and graduate populations. Build the goals, defend the assumptions, deliver the number. Translate the Strategic Enrollment Management Plan into an operational plan with weekly execution and named owners. Present funnel performance, variance, and corrective action to the VP's Executive Council on a defined cycle. Lead net tuition revenue forecasting and scenario modeling with Institutional Effectiveness and Research and the Budget Office. Escalate risk early. The institution can absorb bad news in September. It cannot absorb bad news at census. - (Essential) 25% - Direct undergraduate admissions operations, including application review, decision release, territory design, counselor staffing, travel strategy, and conversion accountability by territory. Direct graduate, online, adult, and transfer recruitment as a distinct operating discipline with its own funnel logic, cycle timing, and conversion standards. These populations do not respond to traditional undergraduate recruitment cadence and should not be run on it. Own the 8Kby28 online enrollment growth trajectory in partnership with Academic Affairs on program supply and Regional Campuses on delivery. Build and maintain transfer pathway and articulation strategy with KCTCS and other feeder institutions, and hold the Registrar to agreed credit evaluation turnaround standards on behalf of transfer yield. Direct dual credit, early college, and college access pipeline strategy. - (Essential) 20% - Direct financial aid strategy, including institutional aid leveraging, discount rate management, scholarship matrix design, and packaging philosophy. Model and recommend aid strategies that optimize net tuition revenue while advancing access for first-generation, rural, and Pell-eligible students. Own federal and state compliance, including Title IV administration, verification, satisfactory academic progress, return of Title IV funds, and Kentucky state aid programs. Compress time from application to award, and from award to student understanding of what they will actually pay. Partner with Big E Central on aid-related navigation, escalation pathways, and case resolution. - (Essential) 15% - Direct the Welcome Center and the full campus visit operation, including daily visits, group visits, counselor-led programming, and the visitor experience standard. Own the recruitment and yield event portfolio, including open houses, admitted student programs, transfer and adult information sessions, and regional events. Establish measurable attribution from visit and event participation to application, deposit, and matriculation. Every event carries a conversion expectation or it does not run. Ensure the visit experience delivers on the brand promise made in marketing. Visit is where recruitment marketing either earns credibility or loses it. - (Essential) 15% - Serve as the primary business owner for enrollment CRM requirements, including application workflow, decision logic, portal behavior, event registration, and funnel communication flows. Submit, prioritize, and defend requirements through the agreed intake process with the Executive Director of Enrollment Systems. Define the enrollment metrics that matter, including funnel stage definitions, conversion standards, source attribution requirements, and territory reporting needs. Enrollment Systems builds and delivers against those definitions. Both parties operate from one agreed set of numbers. Specify data governance requirements from the enrollment side, including source tagging, geographic capture, and student type classification standards, and hold operational discipline within admissions, recruitment, and aid so that data entered upstream is clean. Participate in a standing joint prioritization forum with the Executive Director of Enrollment Systems. Escalate unresolved priority conflicts to the Vice President rather than working around them. Serve as the enrollment-side counterpart to Marketing and Communications, providing audience definition, lead quality standards, and conversion accountability. Brand, creative, campaign, and media authority rests with MarCom and the Vice President. Maintain a working service partnership with the Office of the Registrar covering transfer credit evaluation, registration access for new students, and enrollment data definitions. Partner with academic deans on program-level enrollment strategy, capacity planning, and new program demand assessment. Partner with Student Success and Retention leadership so that recruitment promises match the delivered experience. Manage unit operating budgets and coordinate institutional aid budget planning with the CFO. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 55ac3caa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 3fef61a7 Last Name (required) 641a4bb9 Email (required) 5bb507ed Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States