    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/director-financial-aid-internal-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Financial Aid (Internal)",
      "description": "Director, Financial Aid (Internal) - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Director, Financial Aid (Internal) - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Director, Financial Aid (Internal) 497762 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Director, Financial Aid (Internal) Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: Internal - minimum 5 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 37.5 or more Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G26 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Justin Cristello Job Summary/Basic Functions The Director of Financial Aid performs a variety of duties related to the planning, organization, and direction of financial aid for the university. In collaboration with the Executive Director of Student Financial Assistance, the Director will manage all aspects of the financial aid awarding and disbursement/reconciliation process to ensure compliance with all federal, state and institutional rules, regulations and guidelines. The employee will also supervise and evaluate the performance of assigned staff. The Director handles complex requests, exceptions, exemptions, reconciliation, and reporting as required. The position conducts problem-solving and critical decision-making processes in coordination with other staff and the director to update and improve functional aspects of the financial aid processes. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in finance, business, accounting, or related field is required. Master's degree preferred. Experience: Four years of Financial Aid experience is required with at least 2 years of experience at an Associate Director level. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 40% - Serves as the leader of Financial Aid Program Administration within the Office of Financial Aid •Coordinates and processes Federal Pell and TEACH Grant programs as well as Federal Direct loans and private/alternative loan funds. Compiles and prepares all data, analysis and reporting in a timely and accurate manner. Oversees mandatory reconciliation of funds as well as annual closeout processes. •Oversees several critical Financial Aid processes to include Return of Title IV Funds, disbursement of aid, reconciliation of Title IV and non-Title IV funding. •Maintains oversight for the following sub-units within Financial Aid to include: Financial Aid Systems Processing, Title IV Eligibility and Scholarships and State Aid. •Evaluates, analyzes and interprets Banner operations and makes decisions concerning policy and procedure with financial aid processes. •Supervises three full time staff members – responsible for hiring/evaluation and termination. •Involved with strategic and long-range planning function of the department and division. •Assists with special projects as assigned by senior administrators across the division and campus. •Performs other duties as assigned by the Executive Director. •Coordinates all activities related to Fund Management in close consultation with the Data Analytics Team: Processing, Awarding, Disbursement, Reconciliation and Reporting. •Revises financial aid awards based on changes in enrollment, professional judgements, verification, corrections and receipt of additional aid. - (Essential) 35% - Directs the daily operations of the Office of Student Financial Assistance •Proactively plans and directs the work and priorities of the unit. •Recommends and implements policies and procedures that guide the delivery of services. •Proactively assesses potential administrative, technical and programmatic obstacles and works to address these by adopting or changing policies. •Reviews and interprets federal regulations for financial aid and disseminates information internally to ensure EKU compliance. •Provides backup coverage and assistance to other employees as required or requested. •Assists others in the department to effectively handle workload. - (Essential) 15% - Assists with development of office policy and procedures and staff training •Helps maintain policy and procedures manual to ensure compliance with federal, state and institutional rules and regulations. Evaluates current financial aid policies and procedures and makes recommendations for policy revisions to enhance processes. •Reviews and interprets Federal and State regulations to ensure all financial aid guidelines are being met •Disseminates Federal and State regulations information to departmental staff. •Provides training to the student financial aid staff and the university community regarding financial aid. - (Essential) 10% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned •Provides information for internal and external audits as requested. •Networks and completes professional development activities to enhance knowledge, skills, and abilities. •Cross-trains others and participates in cross-training to enhance skills. •Acts in compliance with contracts, laws, regulations, and University policies, procedures and standards. •Completes special projects and other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 63fa32ab Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) f2de07db Last Name (required) bb809b5a Email (required) 745020a1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospectiv