    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/director-veterans-upward-bound-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Veterans Upward Bound",
      "description": "Director, Veterans Upward Bound - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Director, Veterans Upward Bound - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Director, Veterans Upward Bound 497769 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Director, Veterans Upward Bound Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds Division: 5G0000 - Student Success, Engage & Opp-Restr Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 37.5 Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G22 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Joshua Maynard Job Summary/Basic Functions Oversees and manages services within the regulations set forth by the U.S. Department of Education to assist first- generation, low-income, and/or academically at-risk eligible veterans in eight target area counties to be prepared to succeed in postsecondary education. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master’s degree in education, counseling, higher education, education administration, public administration, or other related field is required. Experience: Three (3) years of related experience in higher education is required, as well as direct service experience with meeting academic, social and economic needs of low-income/first-generation/disabled or disadvantaged student populations. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Veteran Status or experience serving veteran population preferred Job Duties: 40% - Oversee all EKU Veterans Upward Bound program activities, including but not limited to, establishing relationships with service agencies and other external stakeholders and ensuring the program is compliant with laws and regulations. - (Essential) 20% - Supervise and professionally develop program staff. - (Essential) 20% - Develop and disseminate budgets, grant proposals, and other reports and maintain and submit required records of program activity and participants. - (Essential) 10% - Support the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Grant Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c3533d87 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 330975c1 Last Name (required) 7fcd95a5 Email (required) beb40e33 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing a