    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/student-conduct-crisis-management-graduate-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-98236c11-7081-4b19-afa7-20dea048fa9b": {
      "title": "Student Conduct & Crisis Management - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Student Conduct & Crisis Management - Graduate Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Student Conduct & Crisis Management - Graduate Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Conduct & Crisis Management - Graduate Assistant 497779 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant Closing at: Jan 1 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Student Conduct & Crisis Management - Graduate Assistant Position Type: Graduate Assistant Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R000 - University Housing Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Additional Schedule Details: Some nights and weekends required for events Contact Person: Tyler Anderson-Majors Job Summary/Basic Functions Hiring Timeline: All eligible candidates will be contacted via email for an interview, subject to the availability of positions and the selection process. We are hiring for Spring 2027, and the selected candidate will be expected to begin the position in January 2027. Position Summary: The Graduate Assistant for Student Conduct and Crisis Management (GACC) will work out of the Housing and Residence Life office in the Whitlock Building to assist with student conduct, crisis management and other initiatives. GACC will support and implement the Student Code of Conduct Policies and the Residential Community Guide, cultivate standards of care that allows students to grow and develop standard behaviors and enhance the living of all students within our campus communities. The GACC reports directly to the Associate Director of Residence Life for Crisis Management and Residence Life Operations. To view additional information about this position: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wa0-1VqTih_yo1VwbP-038GjRibZOwTXi3ErLqN7b5c/edit?usp=sharing. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelors required. Experience: • Experience in student leadership roles, residence life, or student affairs. • Crisis response, conflict resolution, or supervisory experience. • Strong organizational and administrative skills. • Experience On-call Licensure & Certifications: • Unconditional acceptance into a graduate degree program at Eastern Kentucky University • Enroll in at least nine (9) credit hours per semester in a graduate degree program • Maintain a 3.0 GPA in coursework leading toward the completion of graduate degree • Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills • Possess excellent computer skills (e.g., MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) • Skills in multi-tasking and the availability to work evenings and weekends as needed 2027 • Serve in the on-call rotation for a campus population of approximately 5,000 students, responding to crises and policy violations. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience in student leadership roles, residence life, or student affairs. • Crisis response, conflict resolution, or supervisory experience. • Strong organizational and administrative skills. Job Duties: Work within an assigned focus area within Housing and Residence Life to provide support and development. - (Essential) Perform and support other areas of Housing and Residence Life as assigned. - (Essential) Attend various trainings and meetings as needed. - (Essential) Sponsorship: Position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: For Spring 2027, this role will be a live-on position and will include on-call responsibilities. Continuation of the live-on and on-call requirements beyond Spring 2027 will be subject to the needs of the department and the position. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 5752b178 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R000 - University Housing 77R000 - University Housing Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 4129db03 Last Name (required) 99ab5c9a Email (required) b0497dd7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) a03a9e9e Last Name (required) 1c8e1372 Email (required) d4885f98 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
