    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/graduate-residence-hall-coordinator-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-4998bd6d-70b6-4b9b-99db-2f1d01db86d4": {
      "title": "Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator",
      "description": "Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator 497778 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant Closing at: Jan 1 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator Position Type: Graduate Assistant Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R000 - University Housing Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Additional Schedule Details: Some nights and weekends required. Contact Person: Tyler Anderson-Majors Job Summary/Basic Functions Hiring Timeline: All eligible candidates will be contacted via email for an interview, subject to the availability of positions and the selection process. We are hiring for Spring 2027, and the selected candidate will be expected to begin the position in January 2027. Position Summary: The Graduate Residence Hall Coordinator (GRHC) is a live-in position responsible for supporting the development of a vibrant residential community through student engagement, supervision, and daily operations. The GRHC implements the department’s residential curriculum, focusing on personal growth, community building, and student success. This role co-supervises student staff, assists with crisis response, and collaborates with campus partners to enhance the residential experience. The GRHC reports directly to a Residence Hall Coordinator. To view additional information about this position: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Tw3wzM5Ir_Ce92pmDvxVtPwIRIOIXi05bB0pTbRm9pc/edit?usp=sharing. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: • Unconditional acceptance into a graduate degree program at Eastern Kentucky University • Enroll in at least nine (9) credit hours per semester in a graduate degree program • Maintain a 3.0 GPA in coursework leading toward the completion of graduate degree • Possess excellent written and verbal communication skills • Possess excellent computer skills (e.g., MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) • Skills in multi-tasking and the availability to work evenings and weekends as needed • Possess excellent administrative skills Preferred Qualifications: • 1-2 years prior experience living and working in residence halls • Experience in residence life, student leadership, or student affairs. • Crisis response, conflict resolution, or supervisory experience. • Strong organizational and administrative skills. Job Duties: Co-supervision of approximately 20-30 student staff in their assigned building including resident advisors, community desk managers, and community receptionists. - (Essential) Implement and support community development and student learning through our residential curriculum with intentional interactions, proactive student outreach, and events. - (Essential) Daily management of a residence hall comprised of 300-700 residential students including facilities operations, occupancy management, and crisis response. - (Essential) Collaborate with campus partners to support educational initiatives and living learning communities. - (Essential) Collaborate with campus partners to provide academic support, promote student development, support educational initiatives and develop living learning communities. - (Essential) Serve on the on-call rotation for a campus population of approximately 4,600 students. - (Essential) Participate in a variety of weekly meetings including departmental professional development meetings, departmental business meetings, trainings, supervisory and committee meetings. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1e591fd9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R000 - University Housing 77R000 - University Housing Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) cad48972 Last Name (required) 2b16c448 Email (required) 7a19caba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday s