    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/housing-representative-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Housing Representative",
      "description": "Housing Representative - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Housing Representative - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Housing Representative 497777 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Housing Representative Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R000 - University Housing Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Golf Cart Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Additional Schedule Details: Availability through breaks preferred. Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8.00 per hour Contact Person: Jeanette Crabtree Job Summary/Basic Functions The Housing Representative for the Housing Office will play a crucial role in providing front desk customer service and administrative support to the Housing Office. This position involves interacting with students, staff, and visitors, handling inquiries, and performing a variety of tasks to ensure the smooth operation of the office. Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled at EKU Preferred Qualifications: Knowledgeable in Microsoft Word and Excel. Available hours include Wednesdays from 12:00 noon - 3:30 pm Job Duties: Front Desk Customer Service: o Serve as the first point of contact for students and visitors. o Answer general questions and provide information about housing services. o Collect and process various forms and documents. Phone Management: o Answer incoming phone calls and direct them to the appropriate personnel. o Address phone inquiries and provide accurate information. Administrative Support: o Run errands as needed to support office operations. o Process incoming and outgoing mail, including flyers and packages. o Distribute supplies and maintain inventory. Package Handling: o Pick up packages from the mailroom and ensure they are delivered to the correct recipients. General Assistance: o Perform various tasks to assist the professional staff with daily operations. o Provide support during housing events and activities as needed. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert cf1b42b2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R000 - University Housing 77R000 - University Housing Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 92256a82 Last Name (required) 6f0112ac Email (required) f27afcba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Commun