      "title": "HR Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "HR Student Office Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States HR Student Office Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! HR Student Office Assistant 497767 Richmond Campus Human Resources Positions Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Mar 29 2027 - 23:55 EDT Title: HR Student Office Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 64R000 - Human Resources Division: 4R2000 - Human Resources Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Additional Schedule Details: The HR office is open Monday - Friday, 8:00am to 4:30pm. Contact Person: Krista Caudill Job Summary/Basic Functions The EKU Human Resources office is hiring a Student Office Assistant. The Student Office Assistant will work collaboratively with the Human Resource Operations team to maintain, organize, file, locate, and remove personnel records in the Human Resources office. The Student Office Assistant will also be asked to provide basic front office customer service to ensure the efficiency of office operations. The Student Office Assistant may be asked to assist with projects that may include data analysis, entry, and reporting. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Must be enrolled at EKU. Basic knowledge of Microsoft Excel & other Computer Skills Confidentiality & Compliance with Applicable Laws & Policies Attention to Detail Dependability Preferred Qualifications: Human Resources or Related Field Major preferred. Job Duties: 85% - Maintain, Organize, File, Locate, and Remove personnel records - (Essential) 5% - Front Desk Customer Service - (Essential) 5% - Data entry, analysis, and reporting - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert be52b235 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 64R000 - Human Resources 64R000 - Human Resources Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 1a59001e Last Name (required) f989f4d1 Email (required) 730836e5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overal