      "description": "Associate Vice President, Finance - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Associate Vice President, Finance - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Vice President, Finance 497712 Richmond Campus Financial Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Associate Vice President, Finance Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 01R000 - Sr VP for Finance and CFO Division: 4R0000 - Financial Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G30 Retirement: KTRS Job Summary/Basic Functions The AVP, Finance responsible for analysis and assistance with the maintenance of the University’s general ledger trial balance, revenue/expenditure reporting, cash management services, EKU Foundation operations, financial audits and overall financial management and budget. Responsible for financial/budget oversight and guidance to all auxiliary service operations. Overall management of many University business contracts and administrative units. Select duties will be more defined. Minimum Qualifications Education: B.S. Degree in Accounting, Business, Finance, or other business related, relevant field is required. An MBA and/or CPA is preferred. Experience: Five years or more of appropriate, applicable experience in college/university or governmental business services/operations; and/or administration. Job Duties: 50% - Responsible for analysis and assistance with the maintenance of the University’s general ledger trial balance, revenue/expenditure reporting, cash management services, EKU Foundation operations, financial audits and overall financial management and budget. - (Essential) 30% - Responsible for financial/budget oversight and guidance to all auxiliary service operations. - (Essential) 20% - Overall management of many University business contracts and administrative units. Select duties will be more defined. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 84b7e355 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 01R000 - Sr VP for Finance and CFO 01R000 - Sr VP for Finance and CFO Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 7a874f9b Last Name (required) c85376fc Email (required) 6e664223 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athlet