    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/assistant-director-housing-facilities-operations-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations 497742 Richmond Campus Management Positions Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Participates in on-call emergency response rotation to ensure effective housing operations throughout the academic year, summer programs, and special events. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G22 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Derek Adams Job Summary/Basic Functions The Assistant Director, Housing Facilities Operations supports the overall coordination, administration, and operational effectiveness of University Housing facilities. This position assists with residential facility operations, housing transitions, capital projects, summer programs, operational planning, and departmental initiatives to ensure residential spaces are safe, functional, and prepared to support the student experience. The Assistant Director collaborates with Housing & Residence Life staff, Facilities Management, campus partners, contractors, and vendors to coordinate facility-related operations, communication, and service needs. This position provides leadership and supervision for assigned staff, assists with operational improvements, supports facility projects, and participates in on-call emergency response rotation to ensure effective housing operations throughout the academic year, summer programs, and special events. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business management, Public Administration, or related field required Master’s preferred. Experience: Two years of experience in administration, college student housing or other applicable field. Experience in working with various Microsoft Office products, Banner and Cbord preferred. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 45% - Facilities Administration & Residential Operations ● Assist the Associate Director for Facilities Operations with the coordination and administration of daily University Housing facility operations to ensure residential spaces are clean, safe, functional, and prepared for student occupancy. ● Utilize university facilities management systems to submit, monitor, reconcile, and follow up on work orders, service requests, and operational needs to support timely resolution of facility concerns. ● Coordinate communication and follow-up between University Housing, Facilities Management, custodial services, contractors, and campus partners regarding work orders, cleaning needs, facility concerns, operational priorities, and service requests. ● Partner with custodial services and Facilities Management to monitor residential building conditions, address housekeeping concerns, support quality standards, and ensure residential spaces meet expectations for student living environments. ● Review and reconcile facility-related reports, service requests, and operational data to identify outstanding needs, communicate trends, and support continuous improvement of housing facilities. ● Coordinate operational needs related to housing openings, closings, occupancy transitions, break housing, summer operations, camps, conferences, and special housing programs. ● Assist with furniture moves, room setups, space preparation, labor coordination, and other logistical needs related to residential operations. ● Conduct facility walkthroughs and assist with inspections, operational assessments, and documentation of facility needs and improvement opportunities. ● Assist with processing and reconciling requisitions and purchase orders in accordance with university procurement guidelines. - (Essential) 20% - Residential Operations & Transition Coordination ● Partner with Housing & Residence Life staff to coordinate successful residential transitions, including summer-to-fall opening, fall-to-spring transitions, spring closing, break periods, and other occupancy changes. ● Assist with developing transition timelines, coordinating facility readiness activities, and ensuring residential spaces are prepared for student occupancy. ● Collaborate with Residence Life, Facilities Management, custodial services, and campus partners to communicate operational needs, timelines, and expectations. ● Coordinate communication related to facility impacts, housing transitions, summer operations, camps, conferences, and special programs. ● Provide timely updates and follow-up regarding operational concerns impacting students and residential communities. - (Essential) 20% - On-Call & Operational Planning ● Participate in an after-hours on-call rotation to respond to urgent housing operational concerns, facility issues, safety concerns, and emergency situations during evenings, weekends, holidays, and university closures. ● Coordinate appropriate communication, documentation, and follow-up during emergency situations to support timely resolution and continuity of operations. ● Assist with operational planning related to housing openings, closings, transitions, special events, and facility readiness. ● Develop and maintain operational timelines, coordinate resources, and support planning efforts to ensure successful execution of departmental priorities. ● Assist with security access control and security systems. - (Essential) 10% - Staff Supervision & Leadership ● Provide supervision, training, and leadership for assigned student staff and operational employees supporting housing facilities operations. ● Assist with recruitment, hiring, onboarding, scheduling, training, and performance feedback for assigned staff. ● Establish expectations, assign responsibilities, and provide guidance to ensure effective completion of operational duties. ● Support staff development, accountability, and cross-training opportunities to enhance departmental effectiveness. ● Assist departmental leadership with staffing plans, assessments, and continuous improvement initiatives. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Auxiliary Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert b2b94320 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 206fe83d Last Name (required) 48485b36 Email (required) c5a048f2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School o