      "description": "Education Intern - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Education Intern - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Education Intern 497760 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Oct 22 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Education Intern Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: up to 20 Contact Person: Kelly Watson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Science and Environmental Education Intern will support the Center for Science & Environmental Education in developing and delivering engaging STEM and environmental education programs for K–12 students, families, and community audiences. Interns will assist with educational outreach events, hands-on activities, program preparation, and other Center initiatives while gaining professional experience in science communication, environmental education, teamwork, and community engagement. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU Experience: Applicants should have an interest in science, environmental education, STEM outreach, or working with children and community audiences. Previous formal work experience is not required, but applicants should demonstrate reliability, good communication skills, a willingness to learn, and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to applicants with experience in education, science or environmental outreach, working with children or youth, public engagement, or related volunteer or employment activities. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills, creativity, enthusiasm for science and the environment, and an interest in developing professional skills in informal education and outreach are highly desirable. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible 