    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/eku-guru-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-93c8c547-a263-49ce-a1b5-553e465e63d3": {
      "title": "EKU Guru",
      "description": "EKU Guru - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States EKU Guru - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! EKU Guru 497755 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 21 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: EKU Guru Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 27R100 - Associate Provost-Mulholland Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: Up to 20 Contact Person: Dr. Ashley Sweat Job Summary/Basic Functions The Student Success Center is currently hiring Gurus. Eastern Kentucky University’s Gurus are tutors, mentors, and peer success coaches who are experienced students that help all EKU students professionally and personally. Student employees assist in achieving goals of the programs for the Student Success Center. Those goals are as follows: To provide a supportive environment for students; To assist students in their educational persistence; To serve as a mentor to students; To bring experiences to the team while respecting and valuing other perspectives; To work collaboratively with other EKU student support areas, increase knowledge and understanding of those services, and connect students to those resources; To encourage development of relationships with faculty, students, and staff. Responsibilities: Be approachable and available to meet the needs of students throughout the academic year; Serve as a role model of positive behavior; Participate in on-going training to improve skills and knowledge; Help students become successful academically and socially; Serve as a tutor, mentor, and peer success coach to students for academic, co-curricular, and leadership involvement; Direct students to other individuals, organizations, and programs at EKU related to their interests and needs; Show empathy for students in order to determine their needs; Work in an often fast-paced environment; Be a resource person and referral agent for EKU; Provide information, resources, and workshops for all students. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU. Experience: Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Minimum: Completed at least one semester at EKU, be enrolled currently as a student, and in Good Academic Standing. Student must be self-motivated, take initiative and responsibility, and be friendly and approachable. Desired: Prefer students with a minimum 3.0 GPA. Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ddb4f621 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 27R100 - Associate Provost-Mulholland 27R100 - Associate Provost-Mulholland Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) cf4f4939 Last Name (required) 3d48a89d Email (required) db7543f9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Scien