    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/specialist-collections-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist, Collections",
      "description": "Specialist, Collections - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Specialist, Collections - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Specialist, Collections 497709 Richmond Campus Administrative Support Positions Financial Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Specialist, Collections Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 68R000 - University Business Services Division: 4R0000 - Financial Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Additional Schedule Details: This is an on-campus position. Normal office hours are Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 4:30pm with the exception of some weeks during summer and winter which are Monday-Thursday, 7:30am - 5:00pm. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G20 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Ursula Felicicchia Cox Job Summary/Basic Functions The Student Accounting Services Collections Specialist is responsible for managing processes related to delinquent student Accounts Receivable (AR) and Perkins Loan accounts. This position oversees collection activities through internal efforts, external collection agencies, the Kentucky Department of Revenue, and the U.S. Department of Education while ensuring compliance with applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations. Key responsibilities include tracking and auditing student accounts, monitoring collection activity for accounts placed with third-party agencies, assigning Perkins Loan accounts to the U.S. Department of Education, resolving account discrepancies, and supporting the University's collection and recovery objectives. This role ensures accurate account maintenance, compliance with established procedures, and effective oversight of collection efforts to maximize account resolution and recovery outcomes. The Specialist serves as a primary resource for students, parents, and third-party agencies by providing exceptional customer service and responding to inquiries related to collections and Perkins Loan accounts via phone and email. This role provides guidance, resolves account-related questions and concerns, and supports the Student Accounting Services team in delivering a positive, professional, and customer-focused service experience. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree required. Degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field is preferred. Experience: Three years of experience is required. Experience with student financial services, internal or external collections, and accounting or finance is preferred. Job Duties: 60% - Manages all aspects of delinquent student accounts ensuring Federal regulations and internal procedures are followed and performed at a high level of accuracy. This includes tracking and auditing student accounts, account placement with third party collection agencies and the KY Department of Revenue; processing agency payments and monthly reports, as well as tracking close and recovery rates for the agencies. - (Essential) 20% - Responds to phone calls and emails regarding collection accounts from students, parents, and third-party agencies, providing professional and exceptional customer service while addressing account-related inquiries and concerns. - (Essential) 15% - Maintains the Perkins Loan portfolio and manages account assignments to the U.S. Department of Education, ensuring accurate records and compliance with applicable regulations. - (Essential) 5% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 36f202b9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 68R000 - University Business Services 68R000 - University Business Services Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) f20208c2 Last Name (required) d4d3863d Email (required) fc11c4d3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collabo