      "description": "Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Worker 497751 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 15 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: 10 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Contact Person: Ogechi E Anyanwu Job Summary/Basic Functions 1. Serve as a peer mentor 2. Recruit students for the AFA minor by attending spotlight events 3. Help plan a monthly student and faculty discussion series at the Center and identify panelists 4. Organize and promote AFA/CISE-related events and activities on campus and social media 5. Identify and post educational articles on the black experience on AFA/CISE social media platforms 6. Design and circulate fliers for AFA/CISE-related events and activities 7. Facilitate the AFA monthly spotlight series for faculty, staff, and students 8. Identify opportunities for collaboration with other departments on campus 9. Facilitate “Africana Night Flix” monthly film series 10. Help plan events organized by student organizations 11. Organize biannual career workshops led by AFA alums. Minimum Qualifications Experience: Must be enrolled at EKU Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) 