    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/coordinator-artist-events-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Artist & Events",
      "description": "Coordinator, Artist & Events - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Coordinator, Artist & Events - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Coordinator, Artist & Events 497584 Richmond Campus Hospitality Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Coordinator, Artist & Events Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Division: 3R1000 - Administration and Engagement Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Flexibility and willingness to work variable weekday, evening and weekend work shifts. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G18 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Job Summary/Basic Functions The Artist and Event Services Coordinator, at Eastern Kentucky University, directs the operation of all events across campus, including back-of-house, volunteer and rental operations at Center for the Arts. The Artist and Event Services Coordinator coordinates and oversees artist service details, residency activities and community performances. The incumbent will manage client services, event contract creation and expenses and coordinate activities with others to effectively execute various campus and Center events in compliance with event contracts. The incumbent serves as the on-site manager in charge of back-of-house hospitality operations at all events and represents the University. The Artist and Event Services Coordinator develops and implements event management strategies that encourage repeat customers by creating an excellent overall customer experience. This position will assist with various duties and client services across campus. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's Degree in business management, theater arts, or related field is required. Experience: One year of directly related experience is required, preferably including experience in event planning, customer service, and/or front of house guest service management. Licensure & Certifications: A valid driver's license is required. Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 30% - Ensure an optimal guest experience by directing back-of-house hospitality operations for all Center events. - () 30% - Provide high level performer experience by offering exceptional artist hospitality - () 25% - Coordinate event management activities for all events, ensuring flawless delivery of contracted services and event logistics. - () 10% - Recruit, train, schedule, and manage the back-of-house workforce for the Center. - () 5% - Complete special assignments, act as an advocate for the Center, and do whatever is necessary to ensure efficient operation of the Center. - () Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d214390e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond