    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/specialist-relocation-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist, Relocation",
      "description": "Specialist, Relocation - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Specialist, Relocation - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Specialist, Relocation 497725 Richmond Campus Maintenance Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Specialist, Relocation Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 50R100 - Campus Operations Division: 3R1000 - Administration and Engagement Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (40 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 40 Additional Schedule Details: Overtime as needed Posted Salary Grade: Non-Exempt - G09 Retirement: KERS Contact Person: Magan Lewis Job Summary/Basic Functions The Relocation Specialist's primary responsibilities of this position are coordination and set up of University-related events, including event setup/installation and subsequent take-down/removal of all equipment and materials, including general cleanup and restoration of rooms and areas after conclusion of event. University-related events include but are not limited to events booked by the University's Conferences and Events Center, and other University departments (setting up graduations, weddings, banquets etc.) Secondary responsibilities include delivering items to campus and to departments across campus, such as boxed or pallet shipping. Sometimes off campus pickup and delivery. Pickup and delivery of office furniture, and occasionally resident hall furniture. The Relocation specialist position is a part of Facilities Management that serves the campus community. This includes but is not limited to helping with departments or other facility shops to ensure the campus has successful and efficient outcomes. Minimum Qualifications Education: High School Diploma or GED Experience: One year of work experience Licensure & Certifications: Valid state drivers license is required Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 60% - Completes Daily Work Orders - (Essential) 20% - Event Coordinator/Setup/Take-down: Graduation, Catered Events, Groundbreaking Ceremonies, Dedications, Installations, Homecoming Festivities, Music Events, and other events as directed. - (Essential) 10% - Delivers New and Existing Furniture and Equipment - (Essential) 10% - Provides courier service to extended campus locations - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 359483a0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 50R100 - Campus Operations 50R100 - Campus Operations Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 91fa21b1 Last Name (required) 38b1b0d8 Email (required) e8a34bfb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) dd5039b5 Last Name (required) 089f25a5 Email (required) 1cc73ee4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", 