    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/emc-lab-student-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "EMC Lab Student Assistant",
      "description": "EMC Lab Student Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States EMC Lab Student Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! EMC Lab Student Assistant 497747 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 10 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: EMC Lab Student Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-15 Additional Schedule Details: Must have availability for at least 10 hours per week. Posted Salary Grade: $10.50 per hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Dr. Bill Young Job Summary/Basic Functions This is a student worker position intended to supplement the on-campus EMT and paramedic skills laboratory classes as well as other administrative duties. Applicants DO NOT have to be licensed paramedics or EMTs although they are preferred. Qualified applicants should have the aptitude for teaching and explaining skills to students in initial certification-level courses at the EMT-Basic and/or paramedic level. This is intended for full-time undergraduate or graduate students. Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled full-time at EKU Kentucky or NREMT Licensed EMT Desired but NOT REQUIRED. Kentucky or NREMT Licensed Paramedic HIGHLY desired. Preferred Qualifications: Must submit proof of NREMT and/or state-level EMT or paramedic certification if the applicant possess them. Must have desire to teach/mentor students in clinical settings; preference given to those with FTO experience, precepting experience, and/or instructor/tutoring experience. Must submit proof of current class schedule to prove eligibility to work during lab times. Job Duties: 25% - Assist in maintenance and organization of EMT Basic and paramedic skills labs in various tasks as directed by faculty. - (Essential) 15% - Offer available times to work with EMT/paramedic students for tutoring and mentorship. - (Essential) 10% - Offer available times to work with faculty regarding academic or departmental activities and research - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1f6dbdfc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) aa5ad107 Last Name (required) bb55d509 Email (required) 0be147ed Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing 