      "title": "eSports Lounge Attendant",
      "description": "eSports Lounge Attendant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States eSports Lounge Attendant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! eSports Lounge Attendant 497743 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 20 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: eSports Lounge Attendant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 91R100 - Campus Recreation Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $9 an hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Ryan Pedigo Job Summary/Basic Functions Campus Recreation is accepting applications for eSports Lounge Attendants! Come work at our State-of-the-Art eSports Lounge in the Student Recreation Center! eSports Lounge Attendants will oversee the lounge during their shifts and will be responsible for equipment checkout, the golf simulator, working with patrons and assisting in minor IT activities. The lounge is typically open Monday - Thursday from 11AM until 10PM, Friday from 11AM - 7PM. Shifts are typically broken up into 4 hour shifts, one opening and one closing. Availability will need to be during these hours. There is the potential for other activities and events outside those times. We are looking for quality candidates that have interest in PC and equipment repair, 3D Printing, or eSport event planning. Desirable candidates are motivated to work into a supervisory role. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Must be enrolled at EKU Preferred Qualifications: Basic computer and console knowledge. Ability to use google to fix minor issues. Interest in video games. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and do