    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/gallery-graphic-designer-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Gallery Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Gallery Graphic Designer - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Gallery Graphic Designer - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Gallery Graphic Designer 497741 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 8 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Gallery Graphic Designer Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: 5 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Contact Person: April Pauza Job Summary/Basic Functions FEDERAL WORK STUDY & INSTITUTIONAL APPLICANTS WELCOME. READ ENTIRE JOB POSTING BEFORE APPLYING. RESUMES & COVER LETTERS WELCOME, BUT NOT REQUIRED. Fred Parker Giles Gallery in the Campbell Building seek a student Graphic Designer to assist in the promotional materials for an active university art gallery that hosts a diverse range of exhibitions annually. No previous gallery experience is necessary, but experience and proficiency in design and Adobe Creative Cloud is required. An ideal employee for this job is well spoken, eager to learn, punctual, good communication skills, works well independently and with the gallery director and has a strong understanding of good design. The graphic designer will contribute to a range of promotional duties such as designing exhibition posters and postcards, making designs for social media post for upcoming events, documenting opening receptions and using them for publicity purposes on social media platforms for Giles Gallery. Giles Gallery has open hours Monday-Friday 11AM-4PM. Applicants must have some availability between Monday-Friday from 10AM-5PM to work during open hours. Giles Gallery also has occasional public receptions and artist lectures on Thursday evenings (5:00-7:00PM) and Sunday afternoons (2:00-4:00PM), Giles Gallery Assistants take turns working these shifts and could also document events the Graphic Designer cannot attend. Desirable Skills • Students with knowledge and proficiency of Google Drive, Microsoft Office Suite, and Adobe Creative Suite are encouraged to apply. • Students with experience and knowledge of designing posters and postcards and getting them print ready are highly encouraged to apply. • Students interested in marketing and promotions on social media and print media are encouraged to apply. • Students with talents in event photography, videography and/or graphic design are encouraged to apply. • Students that love being surrounded by art and design should apply! AFTER you complete your application online, email your class schedule to the Giles Gallery Director, Professor April Pauza at april.pauza@eku.edu. Applicants may also upload or email resumes and cover letters (optional), to the same email address AFTER applications are submitted online with EKU HR. To learn more, check out the following: • GG Instagram: www.instagram.com/ekugilesgallery/ • GG Facebook: www.facebook.com/ekugilesgallery/ Minimum Qualifications Experience: Must be an EKU student Preferred Qualifications: • Students with knowledge and proficiency of Google Drive, Microsoft Office Suite, and Adobe Creative Suite are encouraged to apply. • Students with experience and knowledge of designing posters and postcards and getting them print ready are highly encouraged to apply. • Students interested in marketing and promotions on social media and print media are encouraged to apply. • Students with talents in event photography, videography and/or graphic design are encouraged to apply. • Students that love being surrounded by art and design should apply! Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Special Instructions: AFTER you complete your application online, email your class schedule to the Giles Gallery Director, Professor April Pauza at april.pauza@eku.edu. Applicants may also upload or email resumes and cover letters (optional), to the same email address AFTER applications are submitted online with EKU HR. To learn more, check out the following: • GG Instagram: www.instagram.com/ekugilesgallery/ • GG Facebook: www.facebook.com/ekugilesgallery/ EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 8ee9f620 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 6bb163a7 Last Name (required) d0778452 Email (required) 36b98b78 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, an