      "title": "Education Abroad Student Worker",
      "description": "Education Abroad Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Education Abroad Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Education Abroad Student Worker 497656 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 4 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Education Abroad Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 20R000 - Office of the Provost Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-20 Additional Schedule Details: The Education Abroad Office is open Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 4:30 pm during the regular semester. Most student labor hours would be scheduled during the regular office hours with a rare evening or weekend hours for special events. Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Katie Samuel Job Summary/Basic Functions This student position is for employment in the Education Abroad Office. The Student Employee will be answering phones, filing, working on special projects as assigned, and a variety of clerical duties. Minimum Qualifications Experience: At least one study abroad experience. Licensure & Certifications: Must be a current student enrolled at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Creative experience designing posters and flyers and working knowledge of social media platforms is a plus. Strong organizational skills and knowledge base in Microsoft Office products is preferred. Study abroad experience is required. Ability to talk to other students and present to classes is also desired. Job Duties: 30% - Organizing/Filing Paperwork - (Essential) 30% - Peer Advising - (Essential) 20% - Presentation/Tabling/Information Sessions - (Essential) 20% - Special Projects and other assignments - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No AA/EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 6314a125 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 20R000 - Office of the Provost 20R000 - Office of the Provost Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) d0eac734 Last Name (required) f4fc98b8 Email (required) 7dbc2f9f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the c