      "title": "EMC Lab Student Worker",
      "description": "EMC Lab Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States EMC Lab Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! EMC Lab Student Worker 497722 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 27 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: EMC Lab Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - Minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-15 Additional Schedule Details: Must have availability for at least two of the lab meeting days: EMC 110: TR 9:30am-12:45pm EMC 110: MW 9:05 am-12:20pm EMC 342: M 3:45pm-6:45pm EMC 342: W 3:45pm-6:45pm Posted Salary Grade: $16.25/hr Retirement: None Contact Person: Dr. Bill Young Job Summary/Basic Functions This is a student worker position intended to supplement the on-campus EMT and paramedic skills laboratory classes. Qualified applicants must have the aptitude for teaching and explaining skills to students in initial certification-level courses at the EMT-Basic and/or paramedic level. Preference will be given to students who are licensed paramedics capable of assisting both levels of lab classes. This is intended for full-time undergraduate or graduate students who qualify for institutional work study. Minimum Qualifications Must submit proof of NREMT and/or state-level EMT or paramedic certification. Must have desire to teach/mentor students in clinical settings; preference given to those with FTO experience, precepting experience, and/or instructor/tutoring experience. Must submit proof of current class schedule to prove eligibility to work during lab times. Must be a full-time student at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Kentucky or NREMT Licensed EMT Required Kentucky or NREMT Licensed Paramedic desired Job Duties: 50% - Assist current EMC 