    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/specialist-post-award-grants-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist, Post-Award Grants",
      "description": "Specialist, Post-Award Grants - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Specialist, Post-Award Grants - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Specialist, Post-Award Grants 497601 Richmond Campus Academic Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Specialist, Post-Award Grants Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G20 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Anne Cizmar Job Summary/Basic Functions The Post-Award Specialist is responsible for contract negotiation for sponsored projects and post award administrative tasks including budget development support, communicating pre- and post-award compliance concerns, processing award modifications and prior approval requests, providing post-award training and technical assistance to project directors, and completing special projects as assigned to meet the needs of the University and the Sponsored Programs and Research Administration office. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's Degree required Experience: Two years of experience with budgeting, grant compliance, or related duties Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 25% - Develops resources and provides post-award technical assistance to project directors and administrative personnel, including through new award orientation meetings. - (Essential) 25% - Processes subawards, award modifications, and prior approval requests, including scope revisions, budget revisions, and no-cost extensions; functions as a liaison with external funding agencies for post-award issues. - (Essential) 20% - Reviews external award documents to refine the budget, deliverables, and recommend if the contract necessitates EKU Legal Counsel review before the award documents are signed. - (Essential) 15% - Performs general reviews of spending on active grant awards with an emphasis on appropriate allocation of personnel effort and spending trends; communicates compliance concerns for action. - (Essential) 10% - Assists with special projects and initiatives aimed at growing sponsored project funding and improving support for managing awards. - (Essential) 5% - Supports office functions by completing all other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7b2c432d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) ef31c53b Last Name (required) e5559a41 Email (required) ee1e0af0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United