      "title": "Supervisor, Grounds Zone",
      "description": "Supervisor, Grounds Zone - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Supervisor, Grounds Zone - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Supervisor, Grounds Zone 497616 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Supervisor, Grounds Zone Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 50R100 - Campus Operations Division: 3R1000 - Administration and Engagement Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (40 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Overtime as needed Posted Salary Grade: Non-Exempt - G18 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Kyle Willis Job Summary/Basic Functions The Supervisor of Ground Zone is a working foreperson responsible for the completion of assigned grounds maintenance and operational tasks both individually and through direct reports and includes the performance of various tasks as required to maintain a high level of care inside the assigned zone. This position will also be responsible for the oversight of the Elmwood Mansion which includes but not limited to the upkeep of the grounds and will also assist in set up for events held at the mansion This position will also oversee the daily operations of the greenhouse, such as planting, watering, pruning, transplanting, fertilizing and pest control. Monitor and maintain the efficient flow of the overall greenhouse operation with safety and customer service. Inspect plant material for diseases and insect problems. Ensure that the plants have the proper light levels, temperature, humidity, and nutrients. Record data and maintain records for future reference. Oversee that campus landscape beds are maintained. Keep greenhouse organized and stocked with the proper equipment to get the job done in a safe and timely manner. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in horticulture, landscape architecture, agronomy, or related program is required. Experience: One year of related experience is required. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 60% - Overall responsibility to ensure proper maintenance of all grounds areas in assigned zone are being maintained to the required standards at all times. - (Essential) 30% - Oversee and perform any other grounds maintenance tasks to maintain service level standards throughout the year. - (Essential) 10% - Other duties as required and assigned - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d39e9d10 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 50R100 - Campus Operations 50R100 - Campus Operations Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 934c33f9 Last Name (required) 44ddb53b Email (required) c6617dba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for 