      "title": "Assistant Chief Flight Instructor",
      "description": "Assistant Chief Flight Instructor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Assistant Chief Flight Instructor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Chief Flight Instructor 497674 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Fulltime Staff Title: Assistant Chief Flight Instructor Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G23 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Tim Holt Job Summary/Basic Functions The Assistant Chief Flight Instructor assists in overseeing Private, Instrument, Commercial, Multi Engine, CFI/CFII/MEI certificates and ratings in the collegiate Part 141 program. The Assistant Chief Flight Instructor assists in the administration and oversight of flight operation and flight course portions of the aviation program. The incumbent must possess and maintain a strong working knowledge of all applicable Federal Aviation Regulations (FARs) for Part 141 and will assist with all FAA related paperwork and documentation. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree is required. Experience: Two years of directly related experience. Licensure & Certifications: - Certified Flight Instructor CFI, CFII and MEI - Requirements of FAR Part 141 for Assistant Chief Flight Instructor - Possesses and can maintain a 2nd class medical certificate Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 40% - Assists as directed with all EKU Aviation flight training activities. - () 30% - Monitors compliance with the Federal Aviation Regulations (FARs) in the training of students and the supervision of flight instructors. - () 10% - Provides leadership and guidance for flight instructors.