    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-online-facilitator-computer-science-information-technology-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology",
      "description": "Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology 497673 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Feb 7 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: Kuang-Nan Chang Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Computer Science & Information Technology at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for part-time online Facilitator positions, beginning August 2026, with options to renew on a semester-to-semester basis. Part-time facilitators support Faculty Instructors of Record with undergraduate instruction in online courses, including, but not limited to, INF 104. Responsibilities may include assisting students with course activities, providing guidance and support, facilitating student engagement and communication, and working with the course Instructor to support student learning. Course load of up to 9 credit hours per semester, with opportunities at main campus and regional campuses, depending on need. The successful candidate must hold at least an earned Bachelor's degree in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field; or a Bachelor's degree plus at least 18 graduate credit hours in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field; by the time of appointment. Degrees must be from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution. The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate effective communication and interpersonal skills in working with undergraduate students, faculty, and the university community. Review of applications will take place on a rolling basis, given instructional needs and current faculty staffing. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Minimum Qualifications Education: The successful candidate must hold at least an earned Bachelor's degree in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field; or a Bachelor's degree plus at least 18 graduate credit hours in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field; by the time of appointment. Degrees must be from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution. Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Applicant documents Include: - Cover Letter - Vitae/Resume - Copies of Unofficial Transcripts - Contact information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert