    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/bratzke-center-student-tutor-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Bratzke Center- Student Tutor",
      "description": "Bratzke Center- Student Tutor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Bratzke Center- Student Tutor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Bratzke Center- Student Tutor 497654 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 4 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Bratzke Center- Student Tutor Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R005 - Student Success Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Additional Schedule Details: Tutor sessions are by request and matched upon student and tutor availability. Your work hours may vary and are largely dependent on your availability. (Please Note: You will not be able to tutor during your class times i.e if there is zoom scheduled during your class time you cannot tutor even though it is a web class) Posted Salary Grade: $12.00 per hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Sean Hughes Job Summary/Basic Functions This is a position for current EKU students eager to tutor student-athletes in all areas and levels of STEM, Business, English and more offered at EKU. We are actively seeking tutors for the following areas: college skills, science, technology, math, stats, English, Business (ECO, BUS) and other Essential education areas. Students who have strengths in other areas are still encouraged to apply. Students employed in this position are responsible for ensuring the ongoing success of the program by serving as a learning resource for our student athletes and representing the Bratzke Center in a professional manner. Our student employees assist in achieving the goals of the Bratzke Center Tutoring Program by: 1) fostering skill development, 2) encouraging critical thinking, 3) promoting independent learners, and 4) enhancing engagement and collaboration with the academic community here at EKU. These positions work one-on-one with student-athletes. We are currently accepting applications for this position for the Fall 2026 semester. Tutor sessions are by request and matched upon student and tutor availability. Your work hours may vary and are largely depended on your availability. (Please Note: You will not be able to tutor during your class times i.e if there is zoom scheduled during your class time you cannot tutor even though it is a web class) Pay is $12/hour. Should you be considered for the position, you will be contacted by the Tutor Coordinator, Sean Hughes, for an interview. Sean.Hughes@eku.edu Bratzke Center hours are: Sunday: 3:00 – 8:00pm Monday – Thursday: 8:00am – 9:00pm Friday: 8:00am-4:00pm Saturday: Closed Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled as a student at EKU. Undergraduate students Must have a 3.0 or higher GPA and Must have completed at least 30 credit hours Earned at least an A or B in subject area Must be enrolled full time (min 12 credits) Graduate Students Must be enrolled in a graduate level program. If you are a Graduate Student with a Graduate Assistantship position on campus, you MUST have completed 18 credit hours within your program and have a 3.5 GPA to be considered for additional employment. If you are currently a GA you can work an additional 7.5 hours a week with approval from Grad School. Preferred Qualifications: Strong work ethic Professionalism Strong Communication Skills Job Duties: 85% - Tutoring student athletes as scheduled - (Essential) 10% - Filing Tutor Reports via Teamworks - (Essential) 5% - Participate in trainings and professional development opportunities - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: Main areas of need: Business/Math/Stats/Econ/Science/English/Overall college skills Experience working with diverse student population. Ability to work as in person tutor Ability to work flexible schedule and evenings Must provide at least 2 academic references to be contacted to be considered (professor, academic advisor, mentor, current/past EKU supervisor if have worked on campus etc..) EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 4a6dc1f5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R005 - Student Success 30R005 - Student Success Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 52250def Last Name (required) 85ed781e Email (required) c47d3554 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 6126c4c1 Last Name (required) 7e11c63b Email (required) 02f7860d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
