      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture",
      "description": "Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture 497560 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Dec 24 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: Andrea Sexten Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Agriculture at EKU is seeking part-time instructors to teach undergraduate lectures and laboratories, starting Fall 2026 semester with options to renew. Courses may include, but not limited to, undergraduate Agriculture, Technical Agriculture, Animal and Veterinary Sciences, (for majors and for non-majors). Course load of up to 9 credit hours per semester, with opportunities at regional campuses and online modality, depending on need. Candidates must have a minimum of a Master's degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in a related field from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution; Ph.D. preferred. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Review of applications will take place on a rolling basis, given instructional needs and current faculty staffing. Minimum Qualifications Education: Candidates must have a minimum of a Master's degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in a related field from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution; Ph.D. preferred. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Applicant documents include: • Cover Letter • Vitae / Resume • Copies of Unofficial Transcripts • Contact Information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 14d3a2fe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 85eb8b07 Last Name (required) 6beace34 Email (required) aa0ce093 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for develo