    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/director-of-operations-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Operations",
      "description": "Director of Operations - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Director of Operations - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Director of Operations 497634 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Administrator Title: Director of Operations Position Type: Fulltime Administrator Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G26 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Karen Peavler Job Summary/Basic Functions The Director of Housing Operations is responsible for the strategic planning, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive university housing operation, with a primary focus on driving business innovation through data systems and . The incumbent provides leadership for developing responsible, effective, and ethical business practices while overseeing the daily operation of the operations portion of the housing portfolio. The Director of Operations works closely with the Director of Residence Life to ensure all efforts of Housing & Residence Life are cohesive and efficient. Actively serving as the leader of administration, facilities, and technology for the department, the Director spearheads innovation across all housing operational functions. This role leads facilitation and liaises with campus partners on advanced systems configurations, workflow automations, and integrations. Creating data-driven assessments and reports, the Director works to optimize occupancy, streamline central office processes, and inform institutional decision-making. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master's degree in Student Personnel, Business, Finance, or related field is required. Experience: -Three years of experience in developing, administering, and evaluating operations, preferably in Housing -The ability to supervise, motivate, and direct staff while providing organizational leadership Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 45% - Data Assessment & System Administration • Serves as the primary functional administrator within the department for StarRez and other applicable university systems, leading strategic planning, oversight of best practices, user permissions, and module configurations. • Develops, leads testing, implements, and maintains automated workflows within StarRez to eliminate manual processing bottlenecks across all central office cycles. • Liaises with system administrators to ensure data integrity across housing and applicable university systems. Ensure functional integrations and departmental usage of StarRez and campus-wide systems, including Banner, Slate, Lenel, Transact, and communication channels. • Directs the design and execution of online housing applications, roommate matching, room selection, room changes, and housing forms, and any licenses modules, and configurations within StarRez while ensuring responsible data stewardship and adherence to data best practices. • Leverages StarRez and other University data sources and tools to create custom reports to monitor, forecast, and optimize university occupancy and enrollment metrics. • Directs the coordination of physical security and access controls within the residence halls, ensuring accurate access in accordance with StarRez reservations mobile credentialing and security and camera systems. - () 20% - Facilities, Maintenance, & Logistics • Provides leadership oversight for facilities maintenance, furnishings, warehouse operations, and inventory management by utilizing WebTMA and other systems for maintenance and inventory. • Evaluates and optimizes the digital work-order pipeline, ensuring seamless communication between residents, housing staff, and maintenance technicians through integrated platforms. • Coordinates residence hall space management, renovation projects for space needs, and capital improvements. - () 10% - Financial Operations, P3 Oversight, & Budget Management • Forecasts annual residence hall revenue and room rates, as well as evaluating and assessing fee assessment, revenue/expenditures, and financial auditing of records to ensure compliance with university standards and regulations. • Assist with comprehensive oversight and leadership for the housing auxiliary budget operations, ensuring responsible, policy and procedure driven, effective, and ethical financial practices. • Develops strategic plan for residence halls and facilities including a 5-year master plan of building renovations and best practices for building new residence halls. - () 10% - Staff Leadership, Policy Development/Evaluation, Training, & Development • Integrates operational data and StarRez analytics to evaluate policy effectiveness, driving data-informed decisions to improve the student and staff experience. • Establishes, evaluates, and updates all departmental policies, procedures, and SOPs, ensuring compliance with university, state, and federal regulations. This includes the annual assessment of various housing contracts and obtaining legal counsel approval of said contracts. • Provides strategic direction and leadership for staff across operations including administration, facilities, and technology, to ensure a forward-thinking culture of resiliency, innovation, data security, and stability. • Directs and delivers comprehensive training and professional development programs for housing staff, ensuring high proficiency in housing systems (such as StarRez and Lenel), reporting tools, and evolving software/process usage and updates. • Selects, trains, and provides regular goal-setting and performance evaluations for operations staff, aligning individual targets with departmental efficiency goals. - (Essential) 10% - Enterprise Communications • Directs the promotion of the university housing enterprise, liaising with the University Marketing and Communications team alongside the Director of Residence Life and utilizing university systems and CRM tools to deploy targeted automated email/SMS campaigns. • Oversees the strategy, visual appeal, and content accuracy of all departmental websites, portal landing pages, and student-facing communication. - (Essential) 5% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned • Networks and completes professional development activities to enhance knowledge, skills, and abilities. • Attends meetings, training, and other events as requested • Provides back-up on-call coverage and assistance to other employees as required or requested. • Offers to assist others in the department to effectively handle workload. • Cross-trains others and participates in cross-training to enhance skills. • Acts in compliance with contracts, laws, regulations, and University policies, procedures and standards. • Completes special projects and other duties assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Auxiliary Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 74056824 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) c824aba8 Last Name (required) 83dbfe6c Email (required) 1a8e39fd Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) bb4012b4 Last Name (required) 93dea8b7 Email (required) c3088f2c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
