    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/coordinator-fraternity-sorority-life-and-student-involvement-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement",
      "description": "Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement 497632 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Alternative evening schedules are required weekly to account for council advising requirements and for FSL and RSO events. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G20 Retirement: KERS Contact Person: Dr. Shawn M. Dowiak Job Summary/Basic Functions Coordinates and supports the administration of Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement by advising student leaders, facilitating organizational operations, promoting student engagement, ensuring compliance with university policies, and collaborating with campus partners to enhance the student experience. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in Higher Education, Student Affairs, Education, Psychology, Counseling, Leadership, Business Administration, or a related field. Master's degree from an accredited institution in Higher Education, College Student Personnel, Student Affairs, Educational Leadership, or a related field is preferred. Experience: One year of professional or graduate-level experience in higher education, student affairs, student activities, fraternity and sorority life, registered student organizations, campus programming, or a closely related area. Graduate assistant experience may be considered. Demonstrated experience advising student organizations, planning and implementing programs and events, interpreting and applying policies, and collaborating effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills are required. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends and possess or obtain a valid driver's license in accordance with university requirements. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience advising fraternity and sorority communities and/or registered student organizations in a college or university setting. Experience with campus engagement software, student organization management systems, event planning, budget administration, assessment, and risk management. Demonstrated ability to develop collaborative partnerships, manage multiple priorities, supervise student employees, and contribute to initiatives that enhance student engagement and success. Job Duties: 40% - Coordinates and administers Fraternity & Sorority Life by advising governing councils and coaching chapters; assists with recruitment and intake processes; supports chapter development, recognition, and assessment; monitors compliance with university, council, and inter/national organization policies; and coordinates educational programs and community events. - (Essential) 35% - Coordinates and administers the Registered Student Organization (RSO) program by managing organization registration and re-registration, advising student leaders and advisors, coordinating involvement initiatives, maintaining the campus engagement platform, facilitating student organization training, and supporting funding and recognition processes. - (Essential) 20% - Coordinates and assists with department and divisional programs, campus engagement initiatives, and special events; collaborates with campus partners; supervises student employees; and supports departmental assessment, communications, and administrative operations. - (Essential) 5% - Supports the functions of the Center for Student Involvement by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: Please apply with your resume, cover letter, and unofficial transcripts EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 478e8531 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries 77R100 - Student Life Auxiliaries Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) a698c673 Last Name (required) d5dd5dfd Email (required) 6811d8da Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for dev