    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/aquatic-ecology-research-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant",
      "description": "Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant 497648 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 10 Contact Person: robert.pace@eku.edu Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Biological Sciences is seeking a motivated and reliable undergraduate student researcher to assist with aquatic ecology research. This position involves hands-on field and laboratory tasks such as fish collection and identification using seines and backpack electrofishing, macroinvertebrate sampling and identification, and stream habitat assessment . The ideal candidate is detail-oriented, organized, and capable of working independently in a research-focused environment. Must be able to work safely outdoors in warm or cold conditions, lift up to 50 lbs occasionally and carry up to 25 lbs. Prior field and lab experience is a plus but not required; training will be provided. There will be some travel to visit field sites < 2hrs away. This is an excellent opportunity for students interested in gaining practical experience in a research setting. Key Responsibilities: · Collecting and managing data · Proper handling of animals to minimize stress and mortality · Maintaining accurate and efficient record keeping Qualifications: · Currently enrolled as an undergraduate student in a relevant scientific discipline · Responsible, punctual, and able to follow protocols precisely · Interest in ecology, conservation, or fish and wildlife management Flexible hours available during the academic year. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Must be enrolled at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 8cdca2d2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) e7e4d658 Last Name (required) 45a5d116 Email (required) 7b05b9b2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, an