    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/natural-areas-intern-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-7bba3102-bb41-4aab-b91f-3665d5458525": {
      "title": "Natural Areas Intern",
      "description": "Natural Areas Intern - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Natural Areas Intern - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Natural Areas Intern 497649 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Oct 28 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Natural Areas Intern Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Contact Person: Dr. David Brown Job Summary/Basic Functions Natural Areas student employees function to support land stewardship activities including vegetation management, research, community outreach, or other responsibilities associated with our mission. Interns work at Taylor Fork Ecological Area, Cardinal Outdoor Area, Maywoods, and occasionally at Lilley Cornett Woods. Student employees may be involved in assisting Division of Natural Areas staff with any of the following activities: 1. Invasive plant and vegetation management 2. Trail maintenance and repair 3. Wildlife habitat management 4. Assist with environmental education or natural history research projects. 5. Work with community outreach program This is an outdoor position working in rugged terrain and dense vegetation sometimes in inclement weather conditions. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Must be enrolled at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 91cb5881 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) a96c7fdb Last Name (required) 98799659 Email (required) 3fba618b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support spon