    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/associate-senior-associate-athletics-director-of-development-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development",
      "description": "Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development 497608 Richmond Campus Administrative Support Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 81R000 - University Development Division: 7R0000 - Development Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G23 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Sean Hamilton Job Summary/Basic Functions The Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development will be an integral part of the Development and Alumni Engagement team and will also serve as a member of the Athletics Department senior staff. This position will work closely with the Vice President & Director of Athletics to align development efforts with the broader vision and priorities of EKU Athletics. Under the supervision of the Assistant Vice President for Major Gifts, this position will: ● Cultivate, solicit, secure, and steward major gifts ($25,000 and greater). ● Execute a minimum of 12 substantial face-to-face visits per month and a combination of annual and major proposal goals based on portfolio value and tenure. ● Actively engage a prospect portfolio of 80+ individuals/households, working with the Development team, coaches, athletics staff and other campus leaders on unique donor strategies. ● Travel frequently for prospect visits and athletic events, including a minimum of one out of state trip per month. ● Be responsible for recruiting members to the Colonel Club with leadership annual gifts ($1,000 - $5,000). ● Assist with coordination of hospitality areas. ● Responsible for logging metric and contact information into the University system. ● Motivates administrators and coaches to participate in the development process and solicitation of gifts. ● Oversee specific giving initiatives, events, and projects with the purpose of donor acquisition, portfolio building, and donor participation. ● Attend a high number of EKU Athletics games and events, including nights and weekends. Minimum Qualifications Education: A Bachelor's degree is required. Experience: ● Team player with a keen sense of internal and external relationship building. ● Two years of work experience in non-profit fundraising or sales is required. ● Athletics experience and knowledge is required. ● Successful experience in athletics fundraising is preferred. ● Excellent communication, interpersonal relations, and strategic thinking skills; an ability to speak and write persuasively about higher education and EKU. ● Collaborative and transparent with ability to make independent decisions when appropriate. ● Creative, hardworking, and committed to successful fundraising. ● Possesses a high degree of emotional intelligence, diplomacy, and self-awareness. ● Highly attentive to detail. ● Self-starter with discipline in establishing and meeting personal and team goals. ● Mission-driven and identifies with goals of university. ● Ability and willingness to travel and attend numerous evening and weekend events, as required. Job Duties: 60% - Cultivate, solicit, secure, and steward major gifts ($25,000 and greater) by engaging a portfolio of prospects, including frequent travel for donor visits and athletic games/events. - (Essential) 20% - Coordinate with Director of Athletics and Vice President for Major Gifts on athletics department fundraising priorities and on execution of completed major gifts. - (Essential) 10% - Work with head coaches (or their designee) on occasional annual fund events and opportunities. - (Essential) 10% - Other duties including, but not limited to, assisting with coordination of hospitality areas, inputting call reports into CRM, and other administrative duties. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert b4195ffe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 81R000 - University Development 81R000 - University Development Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 2013f0c0 Last Name (required) b0388a8e Email (required) 90f13f09 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) b1fb4999 Last Name (required) e99a392c Email (required) 05221471 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
