      "title": "Accounting Specialist",
      "description": "Accounting Specialist - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Accounting Specialist - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Accounting Specialist 497590 Richmond Campus Financial Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Accounting Specialist Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 60R000 - Accounting & Financial Services Division: 4R0000 - Financial Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 37.5 Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G19 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Angela Burrows Job Summary/Basic Functions A University Accounting Specialist is responsible for timely and accurate analysis, reconciliation updating, and reporting of university information. This information is provided to both internal and external entities. The incumbent also provides technical direction, consultation and customer service to a variety of constituents. Incumbent will work in the Accounting Office. Minimum Qualifications Education: - A Bachelor's degree is required. A degree in Accounting or a related field is preferred. Experience: - No related work experience is required. Prefer someone who has either worked in some capacity with a financial office (i.e. student worker or who has financial education). Job Duties: 80% - Maintains Accounting Records/Reports for the University. - (Essential) 15% - Supports the office functions by completing all other duties and special projects as assigned. - (Essential) 5% - Other Duties as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gend