    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/aviation-student-worker-flight-line-attendant-other-eku-location-kentucky-united-states-0e183ada-d66e-4299-8510-44ee541b93d2": {
      "title": "Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant",
      "description": "Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant - Other EKU Location, Kentucky, United States Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant - Other EKU Location, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant 497624 Other EKU Location Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Other EKU Location Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8.00 per hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Jason Bonham Job Summary/Basic Functions EKU's Fixed Based Operation (FBO) at the Madison Airport located in Richmond/Berea is looking for a Flight Line Attendant. Essential duties and responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned. - Greet aircraft and take service order to include fuel and oil. - Marshall departing and arriving aircraft on the ramp, including both visiting and EKU training aircraft. - Maintain and record appropriate supply levels. - Update arrival/departure board. Communicate customer needs to appropriate departments. - Clean and organize work areas. - Assist line department with wing walking, chocking, safety, and other requests as needed. - Communicate aircraft information via radio, phone, and other electronic devices. - When required, ensure that tie downs, power carts, pre-heaters, and chocks are available to visiting pilots. - Refuel aircraft, as necessary, while ensuring that all fuel charge documentation is provided to the airport manager. - When aircraft maintenance/repair services are required, provide liaison between the visiting pilot and the EKU maintenance support staff. - Provide assistance to the airport manager, as required. - Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Must be EKU student Job Duties: 60% - Towing and fueling aircraft - (Essential) 20% - Greeting customers/customer Service - (Essential) 20% - Building cleaning and ground maintenance - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert f81d98a5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Locations Other EKU Location, Kentucky, United States Other EKU Location, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 08a652ae Last Name (required) c7d45bae Email (required) 45fe2f80 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing