    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/america-reads-tutor-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-434f8bd7-a06a-4aea-9072-765c3b1151c3": {
      "title": "America Reads Tutor",
      "description": "America Reads Tutor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States America Reads Tutor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! America Reads Tutor 497621 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Oct 20 2026 - 23:55 EDT Title: America Reads Tutor Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success,Opportunity&Engage Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-20 Posted Salary Grade: $10 - $15 per hour Contact Person: Cooper Howard Job Summary/Basic Functions Applications will be continuously accepted until all positions have been filled. The student employee will work with elementary-aged children grades K-5 under the direct supervision of a classroom teacher. The tutor will work one on one or with small groups of children. Tutor MUST be able to work in at least two-hour blocks between 8 am to 3 pm on agreed upon days between Monday and Friday. Locations include Model Lab and public elementary schools. (Note: This position is not for clerical duties. Also, if hired the applicant must provide their own transportation to and from the work site). APPLICANT MUST BE ELIGIBLE FOR FEDERAL WORK STUDY. Please review your financial aid on myEKU to see if you have been awarded Federal Work Study. If you believe you should have received Federal Work Study and did not, please contact Big E Central. Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled at EKU and eligible for Federal Work Study. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, p