    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-faculty-philosophy-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy 497605 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Jan 14 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: John Bowes Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of History, Philosophy, and Religious Studies invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach introductory courses in Philosophy and Ethics in-person and online. To be considered to teach courses in our programs, applicants should hold at least a Master's degree in Philosophy. Part-time faculty may teach up to nine credit hours, depending on departmental needs. Applicants will be screened and contacted as departmental needs for part-time faculty arise. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Minimum Qualifications Education: Earned M.A. in Philosophy or related field from an accredited institution at time of appointment. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: Applicant documents include: - Cover letter - Vitae - Copies of unofficial transcripts -Contact information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1cda8bb2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 93d8666e Last Name (required) aca8d004 Email (required) a4416d27 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall f