    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-faculty-dept-of-social-work-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-5c49b2ae-da8c-4383-b00e-b0a66911c357": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work 497595 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Jan 13 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Additional Schedule Details: Teach courses as assigned at the times and in the locations necessary to meet the needs of EKU students Contact Person: Stephanie Saulnier Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Social Work at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach online and in person courses in the BSW and MSW programs. Courses may include, but are not limited to: Introduction to Social Work; Social Work Policy; Human Behavior in the Social Environment and Social Work Practice. To be considered to teach courses in our programs, applicants should hold a Master's of Social Work degree from a Council on Social Work Education-accredited program and must have a minimum of five years post-MSW work experience. Part-time faculty may teach up to nine credit hours, depending on departmental needs. Applicants will be screened and contacted as departmental needs for part-time faculty arise. Applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis. Unofficial transcripts are acceptable at the time of application. Official transcripts are required at the time of the position offer and as a condition of employment. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must have MSW from CSWE-accredited program Experience: Should have five years post-MSW practice experience Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Applicant documents include: • Cover Letter • Vitae/Resume • Copies of unofficial transcripts • Contact Information for 3 Professional References EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d1ea1efb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) a4fed6ec Last Name (required) c72097c6 Email (required) 87eac255 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmos