    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/athletic-trainer-sports-medicine-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-59184d99-ff9a-4ffc-963a-0eb3610f9ae8": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine",
      "description": "Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine 497574 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Division: 6R1000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G21 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dusty Ridner Job Summary/Basic Functions This position is responsible for the prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries to collegiate athletes. In addition, the Athletic Trainer for Sports Medicine administers drug testing, insurance coordination, and travels with athletic teams to all events. The incumbent reports to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine in the administration of a Division I intercollegiate Athletic program in adherence to all university and Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure regulations. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master's degree in Athletic Training or related field is required. Experience: One year of experience in collegiate athletic training is required. Licensure & Certifications: National Athletic Trainers Association (NATA) certification as an Athletic Trainer is required. A State Board of Medical Licensure Certification in Athletic Training is required. A Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure Athletic Training Certification Is Preferred. The successful applicant will obtain a Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure within 3 months if not held at hire. Valid state driver's license is required. Job Duties: 60% - Prevent injuries, treat sports related injuries, and rehabilitate assigned student athletes including taping, bracing, first aid, surgery consultation, medical communication, therapy, and follow up exercises. Monitor environmental conditions. 10% - Recruitment of athletic training students and athletic training managers by attending spotlight days, career days, high school activities / events, and the Kentucky Athletic Trainers Society. Correspond with high school and junior college trainers. 10% - Work with the Bratzke Athletic Academic Center to assist with academic concerns due to athletic injuries or mental health concerns. Also participate within the Athletic Training academic program as a preceptor supporting the academic mission of the Athletic Training program. 10% - Ensure compliance with all applicable laws, regulations, standards, policies and procedures. 10% - Complete all other duties as assigned to ensure the successful operation of the department. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert ed7ace92 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, U