      "description": "Collaborative Pianist - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Collaborative Pianist - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Collaborative Pianist 497568 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Seasonal or Temporary Closing at: Dec 30 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Collaborative Pianist Position Type: Seasonal or Temporary Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 5 - 20 Contact Person: Tim Wiggins Job Summary/Basic Functions Qualified candidates will have a high level of expertise in piano performance and accompanying vocal and instrumental students. The position requires candidate availability to be on campus to play for degree-required courses and recitals. Preference is given to candidates who are able to fulfill accompanying duties during normal work hours. In many cases, work on evenings and weekends may be required. Rehearsal/Performance times will be determined by individual EKU faculty based on course and degree recital requirements. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's Degree in Music Preferred Qualifications: Experience as a collaborative pianist with both vocalists & instrumentalists Flexible work schedule & ability to work during the class times Some evenings & weekend performances Time management, may be working with multiple classes Communication, may need to communicate with multiple faculty to avoid scheduling conflicts Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethni