      "title": "Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff)",
      "description": "Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) 497552 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff Closing at: Dec 31 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) Position Type: Part-Time Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Division: 6R1000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 10-20 Retirement: None Contact Person: Matthew Branham Job Summary/Basic Functions The Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead plays a critical role in supporting and executing the day-to-day functions of athletic facility operations and game/event management. This part-time role is structured to prepare individuals to take full ownership of game operations for select sports (e.g., soccer, softball, baseball, golf, and beach volleyball) after a structured onboarding and training period. Leads work alongside full-time staff and serve as the primary point of contact for designated events or venues. Facility Operations: • Oversee the daily readiness and upkeep of assigned athletic facilities • Coordinate scheduling, equipment staging, and vendor access • Identify and report safety concerns or maintenance needs • Manage digital display systems, including troubleshooting and content oversight • Serve as a liaison between athletics and other departments (e.g., IT, AV, Physical Plant) Event Operations • Lead the planning and execution of game operations for assigned sports • Supervise event setup, staff assignments, crowd management, and post-event wrap-up • Coordinate with officials, visiting teams, vendors, and internal staff • Provide on-the-ground decision-making and problem solving during events Administrative Support • Assist in inventory tracking, supply distribution, and vendor coordination • Manage BSN apparel and Coke distributions • Participate in departmental planning meetings and help mentor Coordinators Preferred Qualifications: One year of relevant experience Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert adb6b42d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 901a9fef Last Name (required) e851ebd7 Email (required) 50e2b0e7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Model Lab School Teacher - Substitute Teacher Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 23R200 - P-12 Programming Model Laboratory School Substitute Teacher - Join the Model family on a flexible basis to help provide world-class instruction to students in the absence of the regular teacher. Executive Director, Marketing Strategy Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy (Deputy Chief Marketing Officer) is a strategic leader, visionary, and operational expert for Eastern Kentucky University’s (EKU) integrated and comprehensive portfolio of marketing, user experience, and digital recruitment initiatives. The Executive Director of Marketing Strategy reports directly to the Vice President of Student Success & Chief Marketing & Communications Officer, serving as the University’s Deputy CMO and standing in for the CMO as needed. The Executive Director is responsible for the development, coordination, and execution of marketing strategies that support brand and reputation enhancement, identity development, and enrollment and engagement results. The Executive Director partners with Enrollment, Academic Affairs, Student Success, University Advancement, University Communications, and community stakeholders to effectively communicate the EKU value proposition through consistent, compelling, and student-focused messaging. The Executive Director will oversee a multidisciplinary team focused on enhancing the digital experience for prospective and current students, managing EKU’s digital brand presence, and implementing data-informed strategies to increase student affinity, yield, and persistence. Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 43R000 - University Outreach & Engagement Student Employees will assist in the day-to-day operations of the Conferencing and Events Department located in the Perkins building. This includes monitoring, working, setting up tech equipment, and office duties. The student worker will also assist the Event Specialists within the department with any event needs. There will be other duties as assigned. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ea7ef148 Last Name (required) 3efe2a0c Email (required) 31245135 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on 