    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/part-time-faculty-clinical-instructor-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor",
      "description": "Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor 497547 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Part-Time Faculty Closing at: Dec 18 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor Position Type: Part-Time Faculty Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Contact Person: Brooke Bentley Job Summary/Basic Functions The School of Nursing at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time clinical position. The part-time faculty position will provide clinical teaching in the Associate of Applied Science in Nursing and Bachelor of Science in Nursing programs. Candidates will be hired from this pool as needed. Applicants should hold a minimum of a Bachelor of Science in Nursing degree from a regionally accredited institution and have two years of clinical experience as a registered nurse. Minimum Qualifications Experience: Bachelor’s degree in nursing from a regionally accredited institution. Unencumbered Registered Nurse license from the state of Kentucky or compact state. Minimum 2 years experience as a registered nurse. Licensure & Certifications: Unencumbered license as a registered nurse in the state of Kentucky or compact state. Preferred Qualifications: -Bachelor or master’s degree in nursing -Minimum 2 years of recent clinical experience in the acute care or public health setting -Experience as a clinical nursing instructor Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does no