      "description": "Pest Control Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Pest Control Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Pest Control Technician 497446 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Pest Control Technician Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 02R003 - Facilities Management Division: 4R3000 - Campus Operations Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (40 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 40 Additional Schedule Details: On Call as needed Posted Salary Grade: Non-Exempt - G08 Retirement: KERS Contact Person: Dixie McHone Job Summary/Basic Functions The Pest Control Technician serves as a utility worker within the Facilities Services Department, performing a combination of functions as needed to properly care for University property and service customers. These responsibilities can include: (1) Ensuring proper treatment and inspections of all university facilities and grounds as well as provision of emergency pest control. All other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Education: High School Diploma or GED Experience: One year of work experience is required. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 33% - Residence Halls, Academic Buildings, Residential Buildings, Off Campus Facilities - (Essential) 33% - Provides response and solutions to emergent situations for pest control related problems. - (Essential) 34% - Maintains required records and ensures compliance with regulations. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation,