    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/senior-analyst-programmer-enterprise-applications-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Analyst, Programmer, Enterprise Applications",
      "description": "Senior Analyst, Programmer, Enterprise Applications - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Senior Analyst, Programmer, Enterprise Applications - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Senior Analyst, Programmer, Enterprise Applications 497236 Richmond Campus Technology Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Senior Analyst, Programmer, Enterprise Applications Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 52R000 - Information Technology Division: 4R1000 - Information Technology Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: 37.5 Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G23 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Jeff Whitaker Job Summary/Basic Functions The Senior Programmer Analyst, Enterprise Applications provides development and support for the university's ERP, web, and digital properties, ensuring a seamless and engaging user experience. This role is responsible for developing, maintaining, and optimizing ERP applications, web applications, integrating systems, and implementing solutions that enhance usability, accessibility, and functionality. The Senior Programmer Analyst, Enterprise Applications collaborates with multiple departments to ensure ERP and websites align with university branding, security, and technology standards Minimum Qualifications Education: ● Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Web Development, or a related field. Preferred proficiency with: XHTML, JavaScript (including SPA frameworks), and CSS; database administration and design with PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server and Oracle; object-oriented PHP and C# programming in conjunction with database SQL programming; ASP.NET Web API; XML programming; working knowledge of content management systems such as WordPress (including custom theme/plugin development), Drupal, or Omni CMS; WCAG accessibility standards; MAMP/LAMP, Apache; Internet browser developer tools; current versions of Microsoft Active Directory Experience: One year of professional experience in web development, website management, or a related field. Experience working in a technical field. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 40% - Web Development & Maintenance - (Essential) 40% - Maintain university application software to maximize efficiency and productivity. - (Essential) 10% - Ensure Data Integrity and Security. - (Essential) 10% - Other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3b150a66 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 52R000 - Information Technology 52R000 - Information Technology Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 3f201cd8 Last Name (required) 707529f0 Email (required) 18897a36 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Ca