      "title": "Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year",
      "description": "Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year 497677 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Model Staff & Faculty Student Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 23R200 - P-12 Programming Division: 3R0000 - P-12 Programming Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: Up to 20 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum of $8.00 per hour Contact Person: vicki.crowe@eku.edu Job Summary/Basic Functions Student workers will support the Model Laboratory School's Early Childhood Development Center through direct oversight and interaction with students following daily activities. The Early Childhood Development Center serves students ages 3-5 from 7:30 a.m. - 6:00 p.m. daily, Monday - Friday, during the Model School year. The program is flexible to accommodate university student workers schedules. Student workers must be self - motivated, able to multitask, well organized, possess superior verbal and written communication and time management skills, able to work in small or large groups (students and staff), and provide help with daily activities and all around supervision. Must be able to meet physical requirements, such as standing, walking, cleaning, or lifting up to 40 pounds. For additional information regarding these student worker opportunities, contact: Vicki Crowe, Model Lab School Early Childhood Development Center, vicki.crowe@eku.edu Minimum Qualifications Must be a current Eastern Kentucky University Student Available for the required hours Preferred Qualifications: The student worker should have an interest in working with children and be energetic, motivated, punctual and organized. Job Duties: 80% - Work under the direction of a supervisor to engage students in indoor and outdoor learning activities, including games, field trips, and working with individuals and groups. - (Essential) 10% - Assist students in your care as needed with completion of basic tasks. - (Essential) 10% - Help to maintain a safe and positive learning environment. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: For this type of employment, state law requires a national and state criminal history background check and a letter provided by the individual, from the Cabinet for Health and Family Services stating the applicant has no administrative findings of child abuse or neglect found through a background check of child abuse and neglect records maintained by the Cabinet for Health and Family Services. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 53a0f0ee Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at 