      "description": "Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison 497676 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 81R000 - University Development Division: 7R0000 - Development Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-20 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum of $8.00 per hour Retirement: None Contact Person: Jessica Duerson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison will carry out daily administrative duties of the division, provide customer service to alumni, donors, students, and potential future colonels, and work closely with the Development and Alumni Engagement team as well as the Student Alumni Ambassador Advisor's to plan, organize, promote, execute, and follow-up all alumni and philanthropic events. Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled at EKU Preferred Qualifications: Flexible Schedule Job Duties: Daily administrative duties - answering/returning telephone calls, greeting and serving visitors, checking mail and voicemails, on campus errands, assisting Alumni Engagement staff members - (Essential) Event planning - gathering, preparing, and organizing event materials, event set-up, event clean-up - (Essential) Maintaining office organization, purging, and conducting inventory of promotional items - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discrim