    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/housing-student-technician-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Housing Student Technician",
      "description": "Housing Student Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Housing Student Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Housing Student Technician 497671 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 7 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Housing Student Technician Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77R000 - University Housing Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: Up to 20 Additional Schedule Details: Fall 2025 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8.00/hour Contact Person: Derek Adams Job Summary/Basic Functions EKU Housing & Residence Life fosters the development, engagement, and success of our residential community by providing an inclusive home that enhances the collegiate experience. The Student Housing Technician serves as an integral component of the EKU Housing & Residence Life facilities maintenance operation. Working in a student residential facilities, the Student Housing Technician will: • Work up to 20 hours/week during an academic semester and may work up 29 hours/week depending on academic course load during break periods. These hours could include some nights and weekends as related to openings and closings of residence halls. • Directly report to the Associate Director for Facility Operations or their designee. • Uphold and follow EKU Housing & Residence Life department mission, vision, and values. • Follow university operational guidelines. • Follow all safety guidelines and practices issued by the university including fit testing for gear. • Wear safety materials and gear as directed by the university. • Assist with the upkeep and cleaning of departmental golf carts and vehicles. • Assist with inventory and delivery of departmental stock and equipment. • Relocate furniture and equipment. • Input work requests to EKU Facilities Management, EKU Information Technology and third party vendors as needed. • Complete a variety of work orders in a timely manner in many areas of a residence hall including student rooms. • Work with campus partners to address department needs and tasks. • Conduct regular maintenance walks of buildings to assess physical condition and maintenance needs. • Assist with the development and implementation of special projects related to departmental maintenance. • Replace electrical outlet covers and switch covers. • Replace room door fire pins. • Conduct repairs on room furniture. • Paint and repair walls and spaces in student housing facilities. • Repair and replace carpet in student housing facilities. • Replace and hang signage, stickers, decals, placards, labels, etc. for the residence halls. • Hang pictures and wall mounted equipment such as boards and electronics as needed. • Repair or replace wall fixtures including but not limited to toilet paper holders, towel bars, towel racks, shelving assembly, etc. • Escort contractors conducting work in residential spaces. • Assist in departmental preparations for new student and returning student move-in days. • Attend all trainings and developments. • Be able to work independently or as part of a team to complete daily tasks. • Possess strong communication and organization skills. • Must able to lift 50 pounds overhead. • Perform administrative duties as assigned. • Complete other duties as assigned by the Associate Director for Facility Operations or their designee. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled as a Full-time EKU student. Must maintain status as a full-time student (enrolled in at least 12-credit hours as an undergraduate student or 9-credit hours as graduate student) Must be in good judicial standing with the University. Preferred Qualifications: Unrestricted, Full Driver's License preferred. Prior experience in manual labor or maintenance preferred, but not required. Can work independently and as a member of a team. Positive attitude towards learning new tasks. Strong communication skills. Provide positive customer service. Job Duties: 80% - Make basic repairs in student rooms. This may include escorting contractors, replacing carpet, and moving furniture - (Essential) 10% - Assist with the development and implementation of special projects related to departmental maintenance. - (Essential) 5% - must be able to lift 50 pounds - (Essential) 5% - Must be eligible to drive university-owned golf carts - (Marginal) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dd25c572 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77R000 - University Housing 77R000 - University Housing Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) de76f170 Last Name (required) e95b7395 Email (required) b7a1c9e7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond 