    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/departmental-office-student-worker-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Departmental Office Student Worker",
      "description": "Departmental Office Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Departmental Office Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Departmental Office Student Worker 497666 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Departmental Office Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: Up to 20 hours Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Contact Person: Beth Taylor Job Summary/Basic Functions The position is one of support to the students, staff, and faculty of the college. Students will work on a variety of different jobs, including making copies, data entry, MS Word, Excel and Google docs and sheets, creating media and putting content on social media, giving information as requested to students and visitors of the college. Assisting as needed on other projects as requested. Minimum Qualifications Education: GPA of 3.0 or higher Licensure & Certifications: Must be currently enrolled at EKU and registered full time. Preferred Qualifications: Applicants should have basic knowledge of Microsoft 365, Google Docs & Sheets. They should have good customer service skills. They should have good social media skills, to promote activities of the college. Looking for someone with a positive attitude, good organizational skills, displays initiative and is a hard worker. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dd4062ca Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 66fc081a Last Name (required) 4e42d498 Email (required) 04eb844b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with 