    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/environmental-health-and-safety-technician-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Environmental Health and Safety Technician",
      "description": "Environmental Health and Safety Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Environmental Health and Safety Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Environmental Health and Safety Technician 497663 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 EST Title: Environmental Health and Safety Technician Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 02R000 - Campus Operations Administration Division: 4R0000 - Financial Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 20 Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Contact Person: Dekia Gaither Job Summary/Basic Functions EH&S Technicians will participate in the Department of Environmental Health and Safety activities including AED inspections, life safety building inspections, laboratory safety inspections, fume hood testing, hazardous chemical inventories, hazardous waste tracking, safety training (OSHA), environmental training (EPA). Technicians will also, upon proper certification, be involved in hazardous waste mitigation activities as well as on-campus transport of materials. The position requires frequent communication in the form of emails, memos, and reports with various University faculty, staff, and students. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled as a student at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Applicants ideally will have at least the following coursework in Environmental Health Science: Industrial Hygiene (EHS 340), Hazardous and Solid Waste (EHS 335), and Air Pollution (EHS 360). OSHA 40-hour HAZWOPER certification is a plus. Strong verbal and written communication skills are desired. Job Duties: 40% - Laboratory Safety Inspections - (Essential) 40% - Life Safety Building Inspections - (Essential) 20% - Email Communication to Faculty and use of webtma maintenance tools - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 56ec5052 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 02R000 - Campus Operations Administration 02R000 - Campus Operations Administration Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 2ddab412 Last Name (required) cbd15acf Email (required) 9fcfe7b9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all ath