    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/program-manager-search-strategy-and-digital-conversion-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion",
      "description": "Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion 497783 Richmond Campus Marketing Positions Fulltime Staff Title: Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: May require occasional evening or weekend work for enrollment events or major digital campaigns. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G26 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dan Hendrickson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Program Manager of Search Strategy and Digital Conversion owns the performance of Eastern Kentucky University's digital environment as a conversion system, from the first search result a prospective student sees through the submitted application. This position owns the full conversion path across both the University website and CRM-hosted student-facing surfaces. Inquiry forms, application portals, status pages, and event registration pages are conversion environments with measurable performance, and they sit on a different domain and templating system than the marketing website. The Program Manager is responsible for ensuring these operate as one continuous experience rather than as a handoff where prospective students and tracking data are lost. This position serves as the University's internal technical authority on search, web conversion, and digital measurement. The Program Manager briefs and evaluates external agency partners, validates their recommendations against institutional academic portfolio priorities, and ensures that agency campaign strategy and EKU digital strategy operate as one system. The Program Manager partners closely with Enrollment Operations, Web Content, Information Technology, Admissions, and academic colleges. Success is measured in cost per enrolled student, organic conversion volume, application completion rate, and the reliability of institutional digital reporting. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Information Systems, Analytics, or a related field is required. Experience may be substituted for the specific degree but not the educational level. Experience: Three years of progressive experience in search engine optimization, web analytics, AI search, or conversion optimization, including direct responsibility for organic search performance on a large website and hands-on configuration of web analytics and conversion tracking. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 30% - Own EKU's organic search strategy across academic program pages, admissions content, and high-intent conversion paths. Conduct keyword, intent, and competitive research to identify visibility gaps against regional and national competitor institutions, including online-first competitors. Establish and maintain technical search standards covering site architecture, page speed, metadata, structured data, internal linking, and mobile performance. Prioritize optimization work and partner with Web Services and academic content owners to implement it. Identify academic programs with demonstrated search demand but no adequate destination page, and drive creation of that content. Monitor indexation, ranking movement, and organic conversion, and report on trends and required interventions. - (Essential) 30% - Own the mapping between search intent and destination page across both organic and paid search, and maintain the keyword to landing page assignment used by agency partners. Hold the standard for whether a page is adequate to receive paid traffic, and diagnose and remediate low landing page experience conditions identified in agency reporting, prioritizing high-spend terms where poor page quality is inflating cost per click. Design, build, and test landing pages, inquiry forms, and student-facing CRM portal pages, including the application portal and status pages. Write and revise search ad copy and ad assets in partnership with agency and internal creative staff where relevance to the destination page is the determining factor in performance. Build and deploy test variants, with test methodology and results evaluation provided by the Marketing and Engagement Analyst. Reduce friction across the full inquiry to application path through form field reduction, clearer page structure, improved mobile experience, and elimination of steps that move students sideways rather than forward. Ensure portal templates meet brand, accessibility, and performance standards. Establish publication standards so that new and revised digital content meets search and conversion requirements before it goes live. - (Essential) 25% - Own the integrity of EKU's digital measurement infrastructure. Define, document, and maintain the University's conversion action dictionary, specifying what each tracked action represents, how it fires, and how it reconciles to a record in the CRM and student information systems. Own tagging architecture, campaign parameter standards, and enforcement of those standards across all University digital activity, including work produced by external partners. Establish and maintain cross-domain measurement between the University website and CRM-hosted surfaces, and ensure source and campaign attribution persists onto the student record so that paid and organic performance can be evaluated through to enrollment. Partner with Enrollment Operations to make application start and application submission reliably measured events. Serve as the authoritative source of data definitions for institutional marketing reporting, and partner with the Marketing and Engagement Analyst, who owns recurring performance analysis and dashboard development, to ensure that reporting rests on verified instrumentation. Identify measurement defects, determine root cause, and drive remediation. Will work directly with paid media vendor on landing pages, conversion optimization, and ensuring seamless integration. - (Essential) 15% - Serve as EKU's primary technical counterpart to external digital and media agency partners. Brief agency teams on institutional academic portfolio priorities, enrollment goals, and program-level context required for sound campaign strategy. Review and validate agency recommendations, including keyword, negative keyword, budget allocation, and bidding proposals, and escalate where a recommendation conflicts with institutional priorities or academic program realities. Evaluate agency deliverables against contracted scope and verify that campaign tagging, tracking templates, and parameter conventions implemented by partners conform to University measurement standards. Maintain a clear division of responsibility between agency-managed advertising platforms and University-owned web and CRM measurement, and ensure no gap exists between them. Consult with academic colleges, Enrollment, and Student Success on digital strategy for program launches and priority initiatives. Provide internal standards guidance and training on search and conversion best practice. Maintain current knowledge of search platform changes, privacy and tracking developments, and AI-driven search behavior, and advise leadership on institutional implications. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert bf1fd5c7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 7fdeeab2 Last Name (required) 0bf092cd Email (required) 9837be1b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Administrator, Systems Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 52R000 - Information Technology The Systems Administrator is responsible for the administration, operation, security, reliability, and lifecycle management of the University’s enterprise computing infrastructure across on-premises and cloud environments. T Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Program Manager of Search Strategy and Digital Conversion owns the performance of Eastern Kentucky University's digital environment as a conversion system, from the first search result a prospective student sees through the submitted application. This position owns the full conversion path across both the University website and CRM-hosted student-facing surfaces. Inquiry forms, application portals, status pages, and event registration pages are conversion environments with measurable performance, and they sit on a different domain and templating system than the marketing website. The Program Manager is responsible for ensuring these operate as one continuous experience rather than as a handoff where prospective students and tracking data are lost. This position serves as the University's internal technical authority on search, web conversion, and digital measurement. The Program Manager briefs and evaluates external agency partners, validates their recommendations against institutional academic portfolio priorities, and ensures that agency campaign strategy and EKU digital strategy operate as one system. The Program Manager partners closely with Enrollment Operations, Web Content, Information Technology, Admissions, and academic colleges. Success is measured in cost per enrolled student, organic conversion volume, application completion rate, and the reliability of institutional digital reporting. Student Enforcement Officer Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 02R005 - Parking & Transportation Student Parking Enforcement Officer Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9e7f8a50 Last Name (required) e20ea8da Email (required) 31bb1d95 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
