      "description": "Student Enforcement Officer - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Student Enforcement Officer - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Enforcement Officer 497801 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Transportation & Parking Positions Student Closing at: Jan 14 2027 - 23:55 EST Title: Student Enforcement Officer Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 02R005 - Parking & Transportation Division: 4R3000 - Campus Operations Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum of $8.00 per hour Contact Person: Trish Jackson Job Summary/Basic Functions This position requires Tuesday and Thursday availability. Student will be responsible for enforcing campus parking regulations, assisting visitors and campus community with parking related questions, setting up cones/barricades for events, working sporting events, and other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Minimum Qualifications Must have a valid drivers license. Must be enrolled at Eastern Kentucky University as a fulltime student. Job Duties: 70% - Parking Enforcement - (Essential) 20% - Event Details - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Auxiliary Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9ec564fe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 02R005 - Parking & Transportation 02R005 - Parking & Transportation Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) f63b3721 Last Name (required) d2cb82f1 Email (required) 159a5d1d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Administrator, Systems Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 52R000 - Information Technology The Systems Administrator is responsible for the administration, operation, security, reliability, and lifecycle management of the University’s enterprise computing infrastructure across on-premises and cloud environments. T Program Manager, Search Strategy and Digital Conversion Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity The Program Manager of Search Strategy and Digital Conversion owns the performance of Eastern Kentucky University's digital environment as a conversion system, from the first search result a prospective student sees through the submitted application. This position owns the full conversion path across both the University website and CRM-hosted student-facing surfaces. Inquiry forms, application portals, status pages, and event registration pages are conversion environments with measurable performance, and they sit on a different domain and templating system than the marketing website. The Program Manager is responsible for ensuring these operate as one continuous experience rather than as a handoff where prospective students and tracking data are lost. This position serves as the University's internal technical authority on search, web conversion, and digital measurement. The Program Manager briefs and evaluates external agency partners, validates their recommendations against institutional academic portfolio priorities, and ensures that agency campaign strategy and EKU digital strategy operate as one system. The Program Manager partners closely with Enrollment Operations, Web Content, Information Technology, Admissions, and academic colleges. Success is measured in cost per enrolled student, organic conversion volume, application completion rate, and the reliability of institutional digital reporting. Student Enforcement Officer Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 02R005 - Parking & Transportation Student Parking Enforcement Officer Graduate Assistant-School of Nursing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 24R000 - College of Health Sciences Graduate Assistant for the School of Nursing Assistant Director, Athletic Marketing Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Marketing is, responsible for developing and implementing creative marketing and promotional strategies that elevate the game day atmosphere, enhance the fan experience, and strengthen student and community engagement. This role plays a key part in supporting the overall brand of EKU Athletics while fostering a culture of excitement, school spirit, and inclusivity across all athletic programs. o Assist in the creation and execution of comprehensive marketing and promotional plans for home athletic events with a strong emphasis on enhancing the overall fan experience. o Lead the development of gameday scripts, in-game promotions, and fan engagement initiatives for various athletic teams. o Collaborate with creative services, communications, ticketing, and event operations to deliver cohesive and high-quality marketing campaigns. o Support sponsorship fulfillment efforts by coordinating gameday activations and ensuring a high-quality presentation for partners. o Provide oversight of student interns. o Work closely with campus partners, student organizations, and residence life to create initiatives that drive student attendance. STEM Center Learning Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 684b77b9 Last Name (required) 3c852ef3 Email (required) 043e6e55 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
